    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Night Seasons"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "You fell in love with Rebecca Dale’s Materna Requiem in 2020 when we gave the North American premiere. Now, joined by the virtuosic cellist Stéphane Tétreault, we’re thrilled to give the North American premiere of Dale’s new work Night Seasons."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/43b2301b-3c1a-4a4d-b5ca-3717a47b596f",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/night-seasons/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/7bd5cd87-f1e5-45f6-a7b1-bb1bcfae5d55",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/WPHeader"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/night-seasons/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/1f4f00ed-6a0e-4992-ba67-6ed05042894c",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/night-seasons/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, March 28, 2026\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave Your Seats\n\n\nRead The Program\n\nAndrew Crustconductor\nStéphane Tétreaultcello\nGreystone Singers/Aurora Voce\nSaskatoon Youth Orchestra\n\n\nFestive Overture, Op. 96Dmitri Shostakovich\nNight SeasonsRebecca Dale\nSymphony No 1 in C Minor, Op 68Johannes Brahms\n\n\nMaestro Andrew Crust made his SSO debut last season, and we instantly knew we needed him back on the podium!\nSSO audiences fell in love with the music of Rebecca Dale in 2020 when we gave the North American premiere of her Materna Requiem. Now, joined by the virtuosic cellist Stéphane Tetreault and choirs, we’re thrilled to give the North American premiere of Dale’s new work Night Seasons.\nEvocative and moving, Night Seasons was the perfect pairing for one of the greatest symphonies ever written. Brahms toiled for years before completing his symphony…and it was worth the wait.\nOnce again taking you on a journey from darkness to light, this concert promises to take your breath away.\nWith an appearance by the Saskatoon Youth Orchestra.\n‘Night Seasons’Concerto for cello, choir & orchestraOriginally commissioned by Koorprojekt Opus, NetherlandsMusic composed by Rebecca Dale © 2022.AII Rights Reserved.\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
