        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/four-seasons/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, September 13, 2025\nKnox United Church\n\n\n838 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 3H4\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave Your Seats\n\n\nRead The Program\n\nJulia Wedmanconductor/violin\n\n\nOuverture and Passepied from Céphale et ProcrisÉlisabeth Jacquet de la Guerre\nSummer from The Four SeasonsAntonio Vivaldi\nSuite from The Fairy Queen, Z. 629Henry Purcell\nAutumn from The Four Seasons, RV 293Antonio Vivaldi\nPassacaille from Céphale et ProcrisÉlisabeth Jacquet de la Guerre\nWinter from The Four Seasons, RV 297Antonio Vivaldi\nVergnügte Ruh, beliebte Seelenlust from Cantata BWV 170J.S. Bach\nSpring from The Four Seasons, RV 269Antonio Vivaldi\nSinfonia from Easter Oratorio, BWV 249aJ.S. Bach, Arr. Alison MacKay\n\n\nRenowned baroque violinist Julia Wedman returns home to lead the SSO in a spectacular celebration of the 300th anniversary of Vivaldi’s timeless Four Seasons.\nThe unique program curated by Wedman explores and complements the seasons in a way fit for a perfect start to our season!\nAdd this show to your subscription package and save!\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
