  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/cbf38aae-dc5f-4439-b3b0-928efdbbc112",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/jeremy-dutcher/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, November 9, 2019\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nBuy Tickets\n\n\n\nJeremy Dutcher\nLucas Waldin, conductor\nPolaris prize winner Jeremy Dutcher is a classically-trained operatic tenor and composer who blends his Wolastoq First Nation roots into his music. Dutcher’s debut album, Wolastoqiyik Lintuwakonawa, involves the rearrangement of 110-year-old recordings from his community. “…if you lose the language, you lose an entirely distinct way of experiencing the world.”  \nA one-of-a-kind music experience, Dutcher’s performance with the SSO is part of his orchestra tour of Canada sharing his artistry with Canada’s classical community.\n \n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
