      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/5b73d351-e791-41c2-974c-47aa8122ae7a",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/sing-along-messiah-2/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n2:00PM, Saturday, December 14, 2019\nKnox United Church\n\n\n838 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 3H4\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nBuy Tickets\n\n\n\nEric Paetkau, Music Director\nDanika Lorèn, soprano\nLisa Hornung, alto\nSpencer McKnight, tenor\nAdam Harris, bass\nSaskatoon Symphony Chorus\nDid you know that singing in a choir is Canada’s national pastime?  More people sing in choirs than any other form of recreation or hobby. And when the music is this good, it’s no wonder why!\nIt doesn’t matter if you’re a professional or have never sung a note before, our Sing-Along Messiah is our favourite concert of the year. There is nothing like a group of people all singing this incredible music to put a smile on your face. \n Don’t want to sing? That’s totally fine! Come and hear a massive choir treat you to the Hallelujah Chorus!\nAll the same incredible soloists as the concert performance, in a slightly shorter performance suitable for families.\nClick here for choral parts.\n\nChoral movements for the Sing-Along Messiah:\nAnd the glory of the Lord\nO thou that tellest good tidings to Zion\nFor unto us a child is born\nGlory to God\nHis yoke is easy\nBehold the Lamb of God\nSurely he hath borne our griefs\nAnd with his stripes we are healed\nAll we like sheep have gone astray\nHe trusted in God\nLet us break their bonds asunder\nHallelujah\nSince by man came death\nWorthy is the Lamb that was slain/Amen\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
