    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/thorgy-the-thorchestra/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Thorgy &amp; The Thorchestra"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Classical Queen Thorgy Thor is crowning the Saskatoon Symphony as her Thorchestra for one night only! Thorgy joins the SSO and Music Director Eric Paetkau for an evening of music and to spill the tea."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/206bc65f-3653-4631-b025-98965340db02",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/thorgy-the-thorchestra/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/9cfcb977-0e90-426b-ad41-f85fbd2a100f",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/thorgy-the-thorchestra/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, October 23, 2021\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nPurchase In-Person Tickets\n\n\n\nThorgy Thor\nEric Paetkau, Music Director\nYou may have heard that you can’t borrow anything from Thorgy, voodoo and all that….so this Halloween, we’re not borrowing, we’re bringing her to town!\nOn top of being a star of RuPaul’s Drag Race, violinist and cellist Thorgy Thor is a damn super star and when we had the chance to return to the stage for our first Pops concert of the year, we knew we needed Thorgy to join us for a night of music, laughs, and tea.\nDid we mention its the week before Halloween? So you better come in costume and be ready for music spanning from Beethoven to Stevie Wonder and back again!\nMake sure you’re looking great and feeling Thorgeous!\n\n[box]The SSO is taking every possible measure to ensure the safety of our audience and musicians at our performances. Proof of vaccination will be required at the door, along with a valid photo ID. Click for More Info[/box]\n\nThorgy & the Thorchestra\nFeaturing Thorgy Thor\nEric Paetkau, Music Director\n\nThis concert features a fabulous collection of tunes we are sure you will recognize!\n \nThorgy Thor\nhttps://www.thorgy.com/\n[box]\nThorgy Thor is a NYC based drag performance artist, event host, TV personality and professional musician.\n Thorgy was a contestant on the Emmy Award winning show Rupaul’s Drag Race Season 8 and Rupaul’s Drag Race All Stars Season 3. She has also appeared on Amazon’s Mozart and the Jungle , VICE, WWHL with Andy Cohen and is a cast member of Dragnificent! on TLC/Hulu.\nThorgy Thor has toured the world with MPpresent Haters Roast comedy tour & A Drag Queen Christmas for the past 4 years. \nThorgy Thor has had the honor of playing solo violin, viola and cello in Thorgy and the Thorchestra with the Pittsburgh Symphony Orchestra, Vancouver Symphony Orchestra, Symphony Nova Scotia, Thunder Bay Symphony Orchestra, Charlotte Symphony Orchestra and has debuted a solo show at Gramercy Theater in NYC in 2019.\n[/box]\n\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\n\nSauvelm McClean, Vocals\nIona Whipp\nStony Mac\n\nErin McVittie, Horn\nPaul Suchan, Keyboard\nAndrew Kesler, Guitar and Bass\n\n\n\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\nWhat’s next at the SSO\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n \n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
