  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/77dcbcef-a8cd-4827-94d2-8b417fa94cfc",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/wolfies-wedding-mozart-reimagined/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n2:00PM, Sunday, March 29, 2020\nConvocation Hall\n\n\n107 Administration Place\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7N 5A2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n\n\n7:30PM, Sunday, March 29, 2020\nConvocation Hall\n\n\n107 Administration Place\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7N 5A2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra, Saskatoon Opera, and FreeFlow Dance are postponing our Mozart Reimagined event on March 29th.\n\nThe decision comes as part of a process all organizations are taking to ensure the safety of the public and our artists during this time.\n\nWe cannot wait to share this spectacular musical theatrical dance experience with our audiences, and will be announcing a rescheduling of the event before long!\n\nYou’re cordially invited to the wedding of\nWolfgang Amadeus Mozart\nAnd \nA Weber Sister….\nHe is certain he’s going to be marrying a Weber sister by the end of the day…the question is, which one…?\nThe Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra is teaming up with Saskatoon Opera and FreeFlow Dance to present a one-of-a-kind event – the performance features the Saskatoon Symphony Chamber Ensemble and the stunning voices of Toronto-based Collectif.\nThe performance features original music of Mozart from his operas Cosi Fan Tutte and Marriage of Figaro.  As well, four emerging Saskatchewan composers (Kendra Harder, Danika Lorèn, Tiess MacKenzie, Alex Tosh) have reimagined the music of Mozart for this special creative project!\nFollow along in this topsy-turvy wedding day with lots of laugh and love!\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
