        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/postcards2/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Paris of the Prairies"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Tying two great cities together in this special concert! Saskatoon has long been called the Paris of the Prairies thanks to our beautiful river banks and passion for culture. Harry Somers' Picasso Suite, Cris Derksen's Five Bucks A Head, and more!\nMasters Series"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/a6889882-02d8-4ede-a7b2-a92f892796a0",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/postcards2/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/37763309-0510-4119-bc9d-54bbc51f372d",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/postcards2/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, October 10, 2020\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\n\n\n602 B 51st Street\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7K 7K3\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nfrom $15\nDigital Ticket\n\n\n\nParis of the Prairies\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nEric Paetkau, Music Director\nA tale of two cities…after our musical excursion to Paris, we knew what we had to musically explore our very own Paris of the Prairies!\nA night of music from prairie composers including Murray Adaskin, Cris Derksen, Jocelyn Morlock, and more. Our beautiful river banks have always made for a great comparison to the city of lights, which gives us a chance to showcase a piece of music that was written for the SSO in 1964 with a Paris connection!\nTo coincide with the opening of the Mendel Art Gallery, the Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra commissioned renowned composer Harry Somers to write a new work that helped celebrate music and art…the work has gone on to be one of the most loved Canadian orchestral pieces ever written. Somers’ Picasso Suite showcases the periods of Pablo Picasso’s life and art through a musical exploration ranging from the avant-garde to jazz.  Now with our very own Picasso collection right here in town, we knew this was the perfect chance to bring a little bit of Pablo’s Paris back to Saskatoon.\nRead the program\n[button link=”https://app.arts-people.com/index.php?show=112223″ border=”#5c1b5c”]Buy a Digital Ticket – Livestream[/button]\n[button link=”https://app.arts-people.com/index.php?buy_pass=saso” bg_color=”#5c1b5c”]Subscribe to the Digital Concert Stream[/button]\nTake a listen!\n\nThe SSO is reimagining the possibilities for what concerts we can bring to the stage for our 90th season and still address the risks and protocols required to ensure safety for musicians and audiences during the pandemic.\nWe’re trying something completely different this year – we’re taking a musical trip around the world, so each and every concert is a musical trip. To ensure that we can keep adapting to the Saskatchewan Public Health requirements, we’re planning trips a month or two at a time. So we’ll be constantly revealing concerts that are coming up!\nEach concert will be available for live stream and video on demand through our new Digital Concert Stream.\nWhile we’re on our musical trips there’ll be all sorts of special travel perks and virtual experiences through our InTune Blog!\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
