        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/postcards3/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A Night at Oktoberfest"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A special night featuring the music from this very musical forest!\nPops Series"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/47fcd956-99bc-4ac5-b81b-eb15f6847ca5",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/postcards3/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/0e918dbe-cf58-42ce-ae77-d4150cd260ba",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/postcards3/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, October 24, 2020\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\n\n\n602 B 51st Street\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7K 7K3\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nfrom $15\nDigital Ticket\n\n\n\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nTime to belly up to the bar for a special night at one of the best parties in the world – Oktoberfest!\n[button link=”https://app.arts-people.com/index.php?show=112226″ border=”#5c1b5c”]Buy a Digital Ticket – Livestream[/button]\n[button link=”https://app.arts-people.com/index.php?buy_pass=saso” bg_color=”#5c1b5c”]Subscribe to the Digital Concert Stream[/button]\nOktoberfest is full of beer and pretzels and great music! So we decided for our falls Pops concert we’d take a musical trip to this incredible party.\nEric Paetkau leads the Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra through Bavarian hits, waltzes, and polkas and more.  We’re thrilled to be showcasing the SSO Brass with traditional music from the Oktoberfest celebrations – they’ll be playing lots of favourite oom-pah music! And we’ll showcase our wind quartet in a very special performance of the Clarinet Polka.\n \nAnd it wouldn’t be Oktoberfest without Ein Prosit!\nMake sure to have you favourite beer on hand to live stream this performance – we’ll make sure to share a good pretzel recipe!\nRead the program\n \n\nIn person attendance for this concert is sold out. You are able to purchase a Digital Ticket to watch the live stream, or subscribe to the Digital Concert Stream to have access to the live stream and concert film on demand.\nThe SSO is reimagining the possibilities for what concerts we can bring to the stage for our 90th season and still address the risks and protocols required to ensure safety for musicians and audiences during the pandemic.\nWe’re trying something completely different this year – we’re taking a musical trip around the world, so each and every concert is a musical trip. To ensure that we can keep adapting to the Saskatchewan Public Health requirements, we’re planning trips a month or two at a time. So we’ll be constantly revealing concerts that are coming up!\nEach concert will be available for live stream and video-on-demand through our new Digital Concert Stream.\nWhile we’re on our musical trips there’ll be all sorts of special travel perks and virtual experiences through our InTune Blog!\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
