  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/9daf81a5-e8dc-4f22-807e-a1429946cc4b",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/candlelight/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, December 12, 2020\nSt John’s Cathedral\n\n\n 816 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7K 3H4\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n$15\nDigital Ticket\n\n\n\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nwith conductor William Rowson\nCasey Peden, soprano\nLisa Hornung, mezzo\nSpencer McKnight, tenor\nA night of Christmas classical from St John’s Cathedral!\nThe SSO is joined by some very special guests to help us bring this intimate candlelight concert to your Christmas season. Nothing is more beautiful than hearing this beautiful seasonal music played in the stunning acoustics of St John’s Cathedral.\nEven though we don’t get to have our traditional performances of Handel’s Messiah, a few of our guests are joining us to bring a touch of Messiah to this beautiful evening!\nOther musical highlights include the music of Bach and Vaughan Williams, and traditional carols like Silent Night, Adeste Fideles, and more.\n \nEach concert will be available for live stream and video on demand through our new Digital Concert Stream.\n[button link=”https://app.arts-people.com/index.php?show=112251″ border=”#5c1b5c”]Buy a Digital Ticket – Livestream[/button]\n[button link=”https://app.arts-people.com/index.php?buy_pass=saso” bg_color=”#5c1b5c”]Subscribe to the Digital Concert Stream[/button]\nWhile we’re on our musical trips there’ll be all sorts of special travel perks and virtual experiences through our InTune Blog!\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
