    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Postcards From Buenos Aires"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A musical adventure to one of the most passion and seductive cities in the world!"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/e423b4b0-8041-417b-9ff9-df6a08a18dbd",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/postcards-from/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/c7e4784b-e37c-4758-a0c8-3ad61b892940",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/postcards-from/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, January 30, 2021\nOnline Event\n\n\n\n$15\nDigital Ticket\n\n\n\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nwith conductor Janna Sailor\nJonathan Goldman, bandoneon\nOur music travels take us to ciudad de la furia!\nBuenos Aires’ wild charm comes to life in this concert of music that highlights the passion and rhythm of what the locals call “el quilombo”. And of course no trip to Argentina would be complete without taking to the streets for a tango.\nWe’re excited to use this concert as a chance to celebrate the 100th anniversary of the birth of one of Argentina’s greatest sons, Astor Piazzolla. His music is captures the imagination of audiences and musicians alike, so we’ll weave this trip through fair winds together with bandoneon artist Jonathan Goldman!\nAnd we’re thrilled to give the North American premiere of music by Adriana Isabel Figueroa Mañas as part of this performance.\nThere’s nothing like a trip to BA, and our live stream brings you the warmth and seduction of la Reina del Plata!\n \n \n[button link=”https://www.canadahelps.org/en/charities/saskatoon-symphony-society/events/postcards-from-buenos-aires-digital-ticket”]Buy a Digital Ticket – Livestream[/button]\n[button link=”https://saskatoonsymphony.org/contact-the-sso/” bg_color=”#5c1b5c”]Subscribe to the Digital Concert Stream[/button]\n\nThe SSO is reimagining the possibilities for what concerts we can bring to the stage for our 90th season and still address the risks and protocols required to ensure safety for musicians and audiences during the pandemic.\nWe’re trying something completely different this year – we’re taking a musical trip around the world, so each and every concert is a musical trip. To ensure that we can keep adapting to the Saskatchewan Public Health requirements, we’re planning trips a month or two at a time. So we’ll be constantly revealing concerts that are coming up!\nEach concert will be available for live stream and video on demand through our new Digital Concert Stream.\nWhile we’re on our musical trips there’ll be all sorts of special travel perks and virtual experiences through our InTune Blog!\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
