        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/nightin/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Valentines from Italy"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A Pops concert perfect for Valentines!"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/b2202cca-6112-4ac9-a70d-f9720123e1f2",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/nightin/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/028d5032-e32e-479a-8db3-abaf0c9bd8b8",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/nightin/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, February 13, 2021\nOnline Event\n\n\n\n$15\nDigital Ticket\n\n\n\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nLeslie Dala, conductor\nKateryna Khartova, soprano\nSpencer McKnight, tenor\nLa Dolce Vita!\nFor this romantic Pops concert we knew we had to take you on a musical adventure to one of the most romantic destinations in the world.\nItaly is full of exceptional food, incredible wine, picturesque views around every corner…and some of the best romantic music ever written. This concert features two Saskatoon rising super stars joining the SSO to bring you love songs like O Sole Mio, Con Te Partiro (Time to Say Goodbye), O Mio Babbino Caro, and more!\nLeslie Dala makes his SSO podium debut, brings his experience and love of Italian music to this performance. You’ll hear love themes from Puccini, the Godfather, dip your toes into the waters of Cinema Paradiso.\nThe evening takes us you on an adventure through from Naples to Rome and across the Italian countryside. You’ll be falling in love with Italy and this passionate music just in time for Valentines!\nRead the Program\n[button link=”https://app.arts-people.com/index.php?show=112235″ border=”#5c1b5c”]Buy a Digital Ticket – Livestream[/button]\n[button link=”https://app.arts-people.com/index.php?buy_pass=saso” bg_color=”#5c1b5c”]Subscribe to the Digital Concert Stream[/button]\n\nThe SSO is reimagining the possibilities for what concerts we can bring to the stage for our 90th season and still address the risks and protocols required to ensure safety for musicians and audiences during the pandemic.\nWe’re trying something completely different this year – we’re taking a musical trip around the world, so each and every concert is a musical trip. To ensure that we can keep adapting to the Saskatchewan Public Health requirements, we’re planning trips a month or two at a time. So we’ll be constantly revealing concerts that are coming up!\nEach concert will be available for live stream and video on demand through our new Digital Concert Stream.\nWhile we’re on our musical trips there’ll be all sorts of special travel perks and virtual experiences through our InTune Blog!\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
