  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/9d94834c-1903-40aa-8c61-b959cfdb28cf",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/constantinople/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Thursday, September 30, 2021\nRemai Arts Centre – Persephone Theatre\n\n\n100 Spadina Crescent\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7K 0L3\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n($32 – $44)\nPurchase In-Person Tickets\n\n\n\nThe musicians of Constantinople, together with Ablaye Cissoko, a griot from Saint-Louis in Senegal, have been wowing audiences around the world since 2012. Pèlerinages Mandingues is the fruit of dialogue and exemplary collaboration between two artists.The show features original compositions by both Cissoko and Tabassian, and revisits pieces from the old Mandinkan and Persian traditions. Join us on our musical journey from the East via Africa to the New World.\nThis exceptional harmony that exists today between our music and our selves has allowed us to create new works inspired by our shared voyages, our shared travels, which we present to you with this concert.\nThe night pays homage to the pilgrim, the one who picks up their staff and goes\n\nThe SSO is taking every precaution it can to keep everyone at our concerts safe. Click for More Info\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
