    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/opening-night-celebration/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/opening-night-celebration/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Opening Night Celebration"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "We're thrilled to be back on stage and celebrating the joy of live music! The SSO is led by Leslie Dala and joined by renowned soprano Danika Loren for this bubbly celebration. Don’t miss your SSO performing the music of Bizet’s Carmen!"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/38f25f3e-0dfb-4657-87ce-173ae380a783",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/opening-night-celebration/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/e9e10f10-b850-4c73-aec4-0a12f61fb1ff",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/opening-night-celebration/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, September 25, 2021\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nPurchase In-Person Tickets\n\n\n\nLeslie Dala, conductor\nDanika Lorén, soprano\nWith great anticipation and careful planning, we’re heading back to the stage and hoping you’ll join us!\nThe Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra opens its 91st season with a musical celebration!\nMaestro Leslie Dala leads the SSO through the passion music of Bizet’s Carmen, the bubbly joy of Bernstein’s Candide, and so much more.\nSoprano Danika Lorén is one of Saskatoon’s most highly celebrated classical artists, and she returns home to perform arias that showcase her world-class voice. At times lush, then quicksilver in boundless coloratura, Lorén’s performances are always show-stopping!\nScroll down to read the program.\nThe performance will be without intermission and will be live-streamed on ConcertStream.tv\n[button link=”https://concertstream.tv/programs/openingnight”]Purchase a Digital Ticket[/button]\n[button link=”www.concertstream.tv/join”]Subscribe to the SSO’s Streaming[/button]\n24 hour live stream tickets for this event are priced at $19.99, $35, $50.\nAll live stream SSO performances are available on the SSO Streaming Subscription, $99 for the entire SSO catalogue.\n\n[box]The SSO is taking every possible measure to ensure the safety of our audience and musicians at our performances. Proof of vaccination will be required at the door, along with a valid photo ID. Click for More Info[/box]\n\n \nThe Program\nOpening Night Celebration\nLeslie Dala, conductor\nDanika Loren, soprano\nMichael Swan, violin\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nOverture to Candide\nLeonard Bernstein\nOverture to L’italiana in Algeri\nGioachino Rossini\n“Je veux vivre dans le rêve” from Romeo and Juliette\nCharles Gounod\nCarmen Suite No. 1\nI.Prelude\nIa. Aragonaise\nII. Intermezzo\nIII. Seguedille\nIV. Les dragons d’Alcala\nV. Les Toreadors\nGeorges Bizet\n“Je dis que rien ne m’épouvante” from Carmen\nGeorges Bizet\nSelections from Carmen Suite No. 2\nVI. Marche des Contrebandiers\nVII. Habanera\nIX. Chanson du Toreador\nGeorges Bizet\n“Dodo, mon tout petit” from Louis Riel\nIan Cusson\nOpera by Harry Somers and Mavor Moore\nMéditation from Thaïs\nJules Massenet\n“Ain’t it a Pretty Night” from Susannah\nCarlisle Floyd\nOverture to West Side Story\nLeonard Berstein\nLeslie Dala\nhttp://www.lesliedala.com/\n[box]Conductor Leslie Dala enjoys a multifaceted career spanning the genres of opera, symphonic music, choral and contemporary works. On the podium, he is known for his passionate, dynamic, and charismatic approach to music making. Named one of the top ten artistic leaders by the Vancouver Sun, Dala’s national profile has grown steadily with guest conducting appearances with Pacific Opera Victoria, Saskatoon Opera, Thunder Bay & Kamloops Symphonies, Thirteen Strings of Ottawa, the COSI Festival in Sulmona, Italy, the Goh Ballet, University of Toronto Opera Department and the Glenn Gould School Opera Program. [/box]\nDanika Lorèn\nhttps://www.danikalorensoprano.com/\n[box]Multifaceted artist Danika Lorèn has not only made a name for herself as a vocalist, but also as a director and composer. Having obtained a masters degree in opera at the University of Toronto, Danika continued training as a vocalist with the Canadian Opera Company’s Ensemble Program from 2016-18. Some of Danika’s signature roles include: Gilda (Rigoletto), Musetta (La Bohème), Adina (L’elisir d’amore), Ginevra/Dalinda (Ariodante), Despina (Così fan Tutte) and Susanna (Le Nozze di Figaro). [/box]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\nEvan Friesen – Violin\nHans Deason – Cello\nThomas Bauer – Flute\nDean McNeill – Trumpet\nWill Martin – Percussion\nMichelle Aalders – Piano and Celeste\nKeri Zwicker – Harp\n\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”10834″]\n \n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
