  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/1d7c4b7a-793c-4ad4-9cb3-0379f458a85d",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/disneys-frozen-film-in-concert/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, January 29, 2022\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nCancelled\n\n\n\n\nThis event has been cancelled. \n\nWe want to ensure the continued safety of our musicians, staff, and our audience, which means we continue to take every possible precaution. At this time we feel as though the right decision is to cancel our January 29th performance of Disney’s Frozen – In Concert Live to Film.\n\n\n\nWe hope that we will have a chance to bring this show back in the future, but for now, we are cancelling which means that we will issue refunds to all ticket holders. We, or the TCU Place box office, will be in touch.\n\n\n\nThank you for continuing to support your orchestra. We hope that this decision allows us to keep going forward with the rest of our incredible season! Stay healthy and stay warm.\n\n \n \nDISNEY’S FROZEN – IN CONCERT LIVE TO FILM\nMARTIN MACDONALD, CONDUCTOR\nSASKATOON SYMPHONY ORCHESTRA\nExperience Disney’s award-winning “Frozen” in a new way with the Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra (SSO). As “Frozen” plays on a large movie screen, Martin MacDonald will lead the SSO performing the film’s score live to film. Tickets are available through saskatoonsymphony.org or the TCU Place box office.\nOne of the most beloved films and soundtracks, “Frozen” features songs by Oscar® and Grammy®-winning songwriters Kristen Anderson-Lopez and Robert Lopez, with score by composer Christophe Beck.\nDisney’s Frozen Live in Concert is produced under license by Disney Concerts, the concert production and licensing division of Disney Music Group, the music arm of The Walt Disney Company.\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
