  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/e143db83-0950-4d11-9283-ab17e73ef813",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/wintersjourney/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Friday, December 17, 2021\nSt John’s Cathedral\n\n\n 816 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7K 3H4\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nIn-Person SOLD OUT Live Stream Access Available\n\n\n\nSSO Chamber Ensemble\nAurora Voce\nCarol Greyeyes, spoken word\nCynthia Dyck, spoken word\nAs the days are nearly at their shortest, we turn to music to bring light into the night.\nThe musicians of the SSO’s Chamber Ensemble bring you a unique exploration of literature and music as we journey towards lengthening days.\nA mix of classical music for Christmas and chamber music that explores the ideas of winter, this concert is an intimate experience that lets us celebrate and reflect.  We’re thrilled to be joined by members of Aurora Voce, led by Maestra Jennifer Lang.\nSit in the stunning acoustics of St John’s Cathedral and soak in a night of beautiful music.\nScroll down to read the program or download a print-at-home copy here.\nThis concert will be approximately 70 minutes in length without intermission and will be live-streamed on ConcertStream.tv.\n[button link=”https://concertstream.tv/programs/live-2h_3jthzkse”]Purchase a Digital Streaming Ticket[/button]\n[button link=”https://concertstream.tv/join”]Purchase an SSO Streaming Subscription[/button]\n24 hour live stream tickets for this event are priced at $19.99, $35, $50.\nAll live stream SSO performances are available on the SSO Streaming Subscription, $99 for the entire SSO catalogue.\n\n[box]The SSO is taking every possible measure to ensure the safety of our audience and musicians at our performances. Proof of vaccination will be required at the door, along with a valid photo ID. Click for More Info[/box]\n\nThe Program\nA Winter’s Journey\nPresented by Nutrien\nSSO Chamber Ensemble\nAurora Voce, conductor Dr. Jennifer Lang\nCarol Greyeyes, spoken word\nCynthia Dyck, spoken word\n*Please hold your applause until the end of the program\nDecember 21, Clear and five degrees\n(Perfectly Still This Solstice Morning)\nfrom Winter Morning Walks: One Hundred Postcards to Jim Harrison\nTed Kooser\nBell Carol / In Dulci Jubilo (Good Christian Men Rejoice)\nTraditional\nArr. Matthew Naughtin\nA Winter Suite\nI. Prologue\nII. Dance\nIII. Interlude\nIV. Finale\n\nThomas Schudel\nWinter 16 from Winter\nPatrick Lane\n\nI Wonder As I Wander\nWords and melody collected by John Joseph Niles\nArr. Donald A. Mills\n\nWinter 14 from Winter\nPatrick Lane\nIn the Bleak Midwinter\nĒriks Ešenvalds\n\nCarol of the Drum\nTraditional Czech Carol\nArr. Matthew Naughtin\n\nJanuary At Roblin Lake from To Paris Never Again\nAl Purdy\n\nWinter Music\nPaul Suchan\n\nAve Maria\nCharles Gounod\n(Based on J.S. Bach’s Prelude in C Major, BWV 846)\nWinter 5 from Winter\nPatrick Lane\nMeditation on the Old Czech Chorale ‘St. Wenceslas’, Op. 35a \nJosef Suk\nYes, Virginia, There is a Santa Claus\nFrancis Pharcellus Church\nO Magnum Mysterium\nMorten Lauridsen\n*Order subject to change.\nSSO Chamber Ensemble\nMichael Swan – Concertmaster\nOxana Ossiptchouk – Principal Violin 2\nJames Legge – Principal Viola\nJohn Payzant – Cello\nChantel Leung – Principal Bass\nAllison Miller – Principal Flute\nErin Brophey – Principal Oboe\nMargaret Wilson – Principal Clarinet\nMaxwell Ostic – Principal Bassoon\nCarol-Marie Cottin – Principal Horn\nSofia Mycyk – Piano\nAurora Voce, conductor Dr. Jennifer Lang\n\n\nJamie Bell\nEmily Coupal\nMicah Coupal\nKieran Foss\nAmanda Friesen\nAndrea Johnson\nDaisy Ko\n \nJordan Kornelsen\nJustin La\nCora Lamers\nMatthew Praksas\nDanielle Strong\nNicole Tremblay\n\n\nClick here to read more about your Orchestra!\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”11091″]\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
