  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/8cdf210d-c734-4019-b011-0222e1af5a67",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/handels-messiah-2022/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/385ebec3-d921-4e98-96bc-e53f85fdf448",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/handels-messiah-2022/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Friday, December 16, 2022\nKnox United Church\n\n\n838 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 3H4\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nBuy Your Tickets\n\n\n\nCosette Justo Valdés, conductor\nMcKenzie Warriner, soprano\nOli Guselle, alto\nSpencer McKnight, tenor\nBrenden Friesen, bass\nSSO Chorus, Duff Warkentin, conductor\n\nJoyous | Reverence | Uplifting\n\nSaskatoon’s longest-running holiday tradition is back! We can’t wait to share the glorious sounds of Handel’s Messiah with you this holiday season.  Cosette Justo Valdés returns to lead four of Saskatchewan’s exceptional vocal artists, the SSO, and Chorus in this timeless work.\nCheck out our Sing-Along Messiah concert right HERE!\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\n\nThe Program\nHandel’s Messiah\nCosette Justo Valdés, conductor\nMcKenzie Warriner, soprano\nOli Guselle, alto\nSpencer McKnight, tenor\nBrenden Friesen, bass\nSSO Chorus, Duff Warkentin, conductor\nMessiah\nPart I\nScene 1: Isaiah’s prophecy of salvation\n\nSinfony (instrumental)\nComfort ye my people (tenor)\nEv’ry valley shall be exalted (air for tenor)\nAnd the glory of the Lord (chorus)\n\nScene 2: The coming judgment\n\nThus saith the Lord of hosts (recitative for bass)\nBut who may abide the day of His coming (alto)\nAnd he shall purify the sons of Levi (chorus)\n\nScene 3: The prophecy of Christ’s birth\n\nBehold, a virgin shall conceive (alto)\nO thou that tellest good tidings to Zion (air for alto and chorus)\nFor behold, darkness shall cover the earth (bass)\nThe people that walked in darkness have seen a great light (bass)\nFor unto us a child is born (duet chorus)\n\nScene 4: The annunciation to the shepherds\n\nPifa\n(a) There were shepherds abiding in the fields (recitative for soprano), (b) And lo, the angel of the Lord (recitative for soprano)\nAnd the angel said unto them (recitative for soprano)\nAnd suddenly there was with the angel (recitative for soprano)\nGlory to God in the highest (chorus)\n\nScene 5: Christ’s healing and redemption\n\nRejoice greatly, O daughter of Zion (soprano)\nThen shall the eyes of the blind be opened (recitative for alto)\nHe shall feed his flock like a shepherd (alto and soprano)\nHis yoke is easy (chorus)\n\n~Intermission~\nPart II\nScene 1: Christ’s Passion\n\nBehold the Lamb of God (chorus)\nHe was despised and rejected of men (alto)\nSurely he has borne our griefs and carried our sorrows (chorus)\nAnd with his stripes we are healed (chorus)\nAll we like sheep have gone astray (chorus)\nAll they that see him laugh him to scorn (recitative for tenor)\nHe trusted in God that he would deliver him (chorus)\nThy rebuke hath broken his heart (tenor)\nBehold and see if there be any sorrow (tenor)\n\nScene 2: Christ’s Death and Resurrection\n\nHe was cut off (tenor)\nBut thou didst not leave his soul in hell (tenor)\nLift up your heads (chorus)\n\nScene 6: The world’s rejection of the Gospel \n\nWhy do the nations so furiously rage together (bass)\nLet us break their bonds asunder (chorus)\nHe that dwelleth in heaven (tenor)\n\nScene 7: God’s ultimate victory\n\nThou shalt break them with a rod of iron (tenor)\nHallelujah (anthem and fugue chorus)\n\nPart III\nScene 1: The promise of eternal life\n\nI know that my Redeemer liveth (soprano)\nSince by man came death (chorus)\n\nScene 2: The Day of Judgment\n\nBehold, I tell you a mystery (bass)\nThe trumpet shall sound (bass)\n\nScene 4: The acclamation of the Messiah\n\nWorthy is the Lamb (chorus)\n\nAmen (chorus)\nGeorge Frideric Handel\nCharles Jennens, librettist\n\nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”11897″]\nThis concert includes:\n\nViolin 1\n Michael Swan, concertmaster\n Jacqueline Nutting, assistant concertmaster\nLillian Jen-Payzant\nJoan Savage\nViolin 2\nOxana Ossiptchouk, principal\nKaren Bindle\nDrusilla Waltz\nKevin MacMillan\nViola\nJim Legge, principal\nSaache Heinrich\nCello\nScott McKnight\nJohn Payzant\nBass\nDavid Humphrey\n\n\nOboe\nErin Brophey, principal\nKevin Junk\nBassoon\nStephanie Unverricht, principal\nTrumpet\nAaron Bueckert\nTerry Heckman\nTimpani\nDarrell Bueckert, principal\nKeyboard\nSofia Mycyk\n\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThe Saskatoon Symphony Chorus\nDuff Warkentin, choral conductor\n\nSoprano                                                      \nLindy Antonini\nKathleen Brannen\nCatherine Berntson\nShelley Bueckert\nHeidi Dick\nSusan Ens-Funk\nJami Gubbe\nAndrea Johnson\nAlto\nJaki Esquirol\nMorgan Esquirol\nKathryn Janzen\nLynette Janzen\nCatherine Klopoushak\nMary Loewen\nShirl Siebert\nElaine Thaller\nJill Wiens\n\n\nTenor                                                           \nPeter Cowan\nRobert Dick\nMichael Friesen\nPeter Hooge\nDerrick Lee\nTyrone McKenzie\nDuff Warkentin\nDavid Woloschuk\nBass\nBrady Anderson\nPatrick Brannen\nEric Chang\nBlake Cumming\nJames Hawn\nJonathan Moore-Wright\nMatthew Praksas\nPhil Siebert\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”11901″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
