      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/e8622d87-179e-4ef3-9f24-6ec09ffd6e45",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/sing-along-messiah-2022/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/f55ff0f4-48c9-4c6f-854f-fc857647cd83",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/sing-along-messiah-2022/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n2:30PM, Saturday, December 17, 2022\nKnox United Church\n\n\n838 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 3H4\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nBuy Your Tickets\n\n\n\nCosette Justo Valdés, conductor\nMcKenzie Warriner, soprano\nOli Guselle, alto\nSpencer McKnight, tenor\nBrenden Friesen, bass\nSSO Chorus, Duff Warkentin, conductor\n\nFun | Community | Relaxed\n\nLove Handel’s Messiah so much you want to sing it from the rooftop? Well, you’re in luck. Join us as we sing along to all your favourite Messiah choruses. Experience the joy of singing as one, or just the incredible sound that comes from so many voices joined together in song. \nWe use the Novello edition of Handel’s Messiah and will have a limited number of copies to lend out during the sing-along. Want to get some practice in ahead of time, or just prefer to read from a device? Use this copy!\nCheck out our Messiah concert right HERE!\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\n\nThe Program\nSing-Along Messiah\n\n1. Sinfonia2. Tenor Recitative: Comfort ye my people3. Tenor Air: Ev’ry valley shall be exalted4. Chorus: And the glory of the Lord8. Alto Recitative: Behold, a virgin shall conceive9. Alto Air and Chorus: O thou that tellest good tidings to Zion10. Bass Recitative: For behold, darkness shall cover the earth11. Bass Air: The people that walked in darkness12. Chorus: For unto us a child is born13. Pifa14a. Soprano Recitative: There were shepherds abiding in the field14b. Soprano Recitative: And, lo, the angel of the Lord15. Soprano Recitative: And the angel said unto them16. Soprano Recitative: And suddenly there was with the angel17. Chorus: Glory to God18. Soprano Air: Rejoice greatly, O daughter of Zion19. Alto Recitative: Then shall the eyes of the blind20. Alto and Soprano Duet: He shall feed his flock21. Chorus: His yoke is easy, and his burthen is light\n~Intermission~\n22. Chorus: Behold the Lamb of God\n23. Alto Air: He was despised\n24. Chorus: Surely he hath borne our griefs\n25. Chorus: And with his stripes we are healed\n26. Chorus: All we like sheep have gone astray\n27. Tenor Recitative: All they that see him laugh him to scorn\n28. Chorus: He trusted in God\n40. Bass Air: Why do the nations so furiously rage together?\n41. Chorus: Let us break their bonds asunder\n42. Tenor Recitative: He that dwelleth in heaven\n43. Tenor Air: Thou shalt break them\n44. Chorus: Hallelujah\n45. Soprano Air: I know that my redeemer liveth\n46. Chorus: Since by man came death\n47. Bass Recitative: Behold, I tell you a mystery\n48. Bass Air: The trumpet shall sound\n53. Chorus: Worthy is the Lamb that was slain/Amen\nGeorge Frideric Handel\nCharles Jennens, librettist\n\nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”11897″]\nThis concert includes:\n\nViolin 1\n Michael Swan, concertmaster\n Jacqueline Nutting, assistant concertmaster\nLillian Jen-Payzant\nJoan Savage\nViolin 2\nOxana Ossiptchouk, principal\nKaren Bindle\nDrusilla Waltz\nKevin MacMillan\nViola\nJim Legge, principal\nSaache Heinrich\nCello\nScott McKnight\nJohn Payzant\nBass\nDavid Humphrey\n\n\nOboe\nErin Brophey, principal\nKevin Junk\nBassoon\nStephanie Unverricht, principal\nTrumpet\nAaron Bueckert\nTerry Heckman\nTimpani\nDarrell Bueckert, principal\nKeyboard\nSofia Mycyk\n\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThe Saskatoon Symphony Chorus\nDuff Warkentin, choral conductor\n\nSoprano                                                      \nLindy Antonini\nKathleen Brannen\nCatherine Berntson\nShelley Bueckert\nHeidi Dick\nSusan Ens-Funk\nJami Gubbe\nAndrea Johnson\nAlto\nJaki Esquirol\nMorgan Esquirol\nKathryn Janzen\nLynette Janzen\nCatherine Klopoushak\nMary Loewen\nShirl Siebert\nElaine Thaller\nJill Wiens\n\n\nTenor                                                           \nPeter Cowan\nRobert Dick\nMichael Friesen\nPeter Hooge\nDerrick Lee\nTyrone McKenzie\nDuff Warkentin\nDavid Woloschuk\nBass\nBrady Anderson\nPatrick Brannen\nEric Chang\nBlake Cumming\nJames Hawn\nJonathan Moore-Wright\nMatthew Praksas\nPhil Siebert\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”11901″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
