  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/dc79f363-5bd9-4168-9010-bac9fc3c1612",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/baroque-soul/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, May 27, 2023\nSt John’s Cathedral\n\n\n 816 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7K 3H4\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nBuy Your Tickets\n\n\n\nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nAlexa Haynes-Pilon, cello\nOverture-Suite “La Bourse” TWV 55:B11 – Georg Philipp Telemann\nConcerto for Cello in G Minor, RV 416 – Antonio Vivaldi\nConcerto Grosso No. 2 in B-flat Major, Op. 3, HWV 313 – George Frideric Handel\nLe Bourgeois Gentilhomme, LWV 43 – Jean-Baptiste Lully\nConcerto Grosso No. 7 in B-flat Major, Op. 6, HWV 325 – George Frideric Handel\nCello Concerto No. 2 in D Minor, L. 60 – Leonardo Leo\nSinfonie Conclusion, TWV 50:5 – Georg Philipp Telemann\n\nPassion | Inspirational | Soulfulness\nScroll down to read the full program or click here to download a copy.\n\nSaskatoon’s own Alexa Haynes-Pilon has quickly established herself in the early music scene and is known for her brilliance on baroque cello, viola de gamba, and even baroque bassoon. She returns home to the prairies to lead your orchestra with her cello in a program of early music that gives us a glimpse into concert halls of the 17th century. It’s a chance to be immersed in some truly timeless classics.\n \nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nA digital ticket gives you 24-hour access to the stream for $19.99\nSupporter tickets can be purchased for $35 and $50\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\n\nThe Program\nBaroque Soul\nAlexa Haynes-Pilon, cello\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\n\n\nOverture-Suite “La Bourse” TWV 55:B11\nI. Ouverture\nII. Le répos interrompu – avec douceur\nIII. La guerre en la paix\nIV. Les Vainqueurs vaincus\nV. La Solitude associée\nVI. L’Espérance de Missisippi – Vivement\n\nGeorg Philipp Telemann\nConcerto for Cello in G Minor, RV 416\nI. Allegro\nII. Adagio\nIII. Allegro\nAntonio Vivaldi\nConcerto Grosso No. 2 in B-flat Major, Op. 3, HWV 313\nI. Vivace\nII. Largo\nIII. Allegro\nIV. Menuet\nV. Gavotte\n\nGeorge Frideric Handel\nLe Bourgeois Gentilhomme, LWV 43\n11. Marche pour la Cérémonie des Turcs\n10. Chaconne des Scaramouches\n\nJean-Baptiste Lully\n~Intermission~\nConcerto Grosso No. 7 in B-flat Major, Op. 6, HWV 325\nI. Largo\nII. Allegro\nIII. Largo e piano\nIV. Andante\nV. Hornpipe\n\nGeorge Frideric Handel\nCello Concerto No. 2 in D Minor, L. 60\nI. Andante grazioso\nII. Con spirito\nIII. Amoroso\nIV. Allegro\n\nLeonardo Leo\nSinfonie Conclusion, TWV 50:5\nGeorg Philipp Telemann\nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”12327″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\n\nHarpsichord  –  Christina Hutten\n*Special thanks to Gary Day for the use of his harpsichord!*\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”12326″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
