  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/7721b7df-c2e8-4fd9-aba8-a1647bb50802",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/mujer/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n2:30PM, Sunday, October 16, 2022\nSt John’s Cathedral\n\n\n 816 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7K 3H4\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nBuy Your Tickets\n\n\n\nCosette Justo Valdés, conductor\nCasey Peden, soprano\nLisa Hornung, contralto\nSpencer McKnight, tenor\nJordie Hughton, bass\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra Chorus\nDuff Warkentin, Chorus Conductor\nLeyendas: An Andean Walkabout – Gabriela Lena Frank\nDixit Dominus – Marianna Martines\nRebelión – Evelin Ramón\nEntr’acte – Caroline Shaw\n\nOptimism | Joy | Powerful\nCosette Justo Valdés has led orchestras in her home country of Cuba, in Europe, and now, lucky for us, in Canada. Her unique style and contagious amounts of energy bring new and refreshing interpretations to every performance. She leads the SSO and Chorus in the Canadian premiere of Marianna Martines’s Dixit Dominus.\nThe concert also includes the world premiere of Evelin Ramón’s brand-new work Rebelión and featured works by Caroline Shaw and Gabriela Lena Frank.\n Scroll down to read the full program. You can download the print-at-home version here.\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\nThe Program\nMujer\nCosette Justo Valdés, conductor\nCasey Peden, soprano\nLisa Hornung, contralto\nSpencer McKnight, tenor\nJordie Hughton, bass\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra Chorus\nDuff Warkentin, Chorus Conductor\n \nLeyendas: An Andean Walkabout\nI. Toyos\nII. Tarqueada\nIV. Chasqui\n\nGabriela Lena Frank\nRebelión\nEvelin Ramón\nLa création de cette oevre a été rendue possible grâce à l’appui financier du Conseil des arts et des lettres du Québec.\n~Intermission~\nEntr’acte\nCaroline Shaw\nDixit Dominus\nI. Dixit Dominus\nII. Virgam virtutis tuae\nIII. Tecum principium\nIV. Juravit Dominus\nV. Dominus a dextris tuis\nVI. Gloria Patri\nVII. Et in saecula\n\nMarianna Martines\nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”11776″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\nCello – Terry Sturge\nFlute – Jennifer McAllister\nOboe – Carl Hofmeister\nPiano – Michelle Aalders\n\nSoprano 1\nKathleen Brannen\nMegan Grier\nJami Gubbe\nBarb Milner\n\nSoprano 2\nShelley Bueckert\nHeidi Dick\nSusan Ens Funk\nAndrea Johnson\n\nAlto\nKendra Harder\nKathryn Janzen\nShirl Siebert\nElaine Thaller\nJill Wiens\n\n\nTenor\nTim Bangsund\nPeter Cowan\nMichael Friesen\nPeter Hooge\nDerrick Lee\nTyrone McKenzie\n\nBass\nBrady Anderson\nErich Chang\nBlake Cumming\nJames Hawn\nJonathan Moore-Wright\nMatthew Praksas\nPhil Siebert\n\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”11772″]\nWhat’s Next\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
