  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/a8820a60-20dd-4ecc-b102-126212a6ee8c",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/idea-of-north/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, February 11, 2023\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nBuy Your Tickets\n\n\n\nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\nRune Bergmann, conductor\nJan Lisiecki, piano\n\nPiano Concerto in A minor, Op. 16 – Edvard Grieg\nSymphony No. 1 in E minor, Op. 39 – Jean Sibelius\nScroll down to read the full program or click here to download the print-at-home version.\n(Please note program order has changed since the time of printing.)\n\nExhilarating | Dramatic | Stirring \n\nJan Lisiecki has established himself as one of the greatest pianists alive today. After his incredible recital last season he returns to play with the full power of your SSO! We are thrilled that internationally acclaimed conductor Rune Bergmann joins us at the podium for Grieg’s Piano Concerto and Sibelius’ Symphony No. 1. It’s a night you won’t forget.\nThis concert is a part of our Northern Lights Festival.\n \nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nThis concert is available for live streaming to ConcertStream subscribers only.\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\n\n\nThe Program\nIdea of North\nRune Bergmann, conductor\nJan Lisiecki, piano\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\n \nSymphony No. 1, Op.39\n\nAndante, ma non troppo – Allegro energico\nAndante (ma non troppo lento)\nScherzo: Allegro\nFinale: Andante – Allegro molto\n\nJean Sibelius\n~Intermission~\nPiano Concerto in A minor, Op. 16\n\nAllegro molto moderato\nAdagio\nAllegro moderato molto e marcato\n\nEdvard Grieg\nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”11998″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\n\nViolin 1- Luke Hnenny, Nova Wong, Richard Wang\nViolin 2 – Evan Friesen, Monica Martin\nCello – Terry Sturge\nOboe – Carl Hoffmeister\nTrumpet – Dean McNeill\nHarp – Keri Zwicker\n\n\n\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”11999″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
