  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/363425dc-e347-4ef3-beb8-7987c6102595",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/bolero/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, November 19, 2022\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nBuy Your Tickets\n\n\n\nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\nJudith Yan, conductor\nAngela Cheng, piano\nLa Vida Breve – Manuel de Falla (Interlude/Dance No. 1)\nNights in the Gardens of Spain, G. 49 – Manuel de Falla\nViento del oeste – Fernando Velázquez\nBoléro – Maurice Ravel\nPassionate | Fiery | Sensual\nDance the night away with pianist Angela Cheng and the SSO. Her show-stopping performance of de Falla’s Nights in the Gardens of Spain will intoxicate you. We’ll crisscross Spain in a musical adventure featuring music from La Vida Breve, Fernando Velázquez’ Viento del oeste, and Ravel’s sensuous Boléro.\nScroll down to read the full program. You can download the print-at-home version here.\nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nA digital ticket gives you 24-hour access to the stream for $19.99\nSupporter tickets can be purchased for $35 and $50\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\nThe Program\nBolero!\nJudith Yan, conductor\nAngela Cheng, piano\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\n“Interludio e Danza” from La vida breve\nManuel de Falla\nNoches en los Jardines de España (“Nights in the Gardens of Spain”)\n\n En el Generalife (“In the Generalife”)\n Danza Lejana (“Distant Dance”)\nEn los Jardines de la Sierra de Córdoba (“In the Gardens of the Mountains of Córdoba”)\n\nManuel de Falla\n~Intermission~\nViento del oeste (“The West Wind”)\n\n Andante (Walk)\n Contemplation – Still\nAnimato – Celebration\n\nFernando Velázquez\nBolero\nMaurice Ravel\nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”11831″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\n\nViolin 1 – Lauren Dykstra, Sofia Mycyk, Alexa Arnyek\nViolin 2 – Richard Wang\nCello – Terry Sturge, Zaide Masich\nFlute/Piccolo – Jennifer McAllister\nOboe – Tyrell Hardlotte\nBass Clarinet – Alyssa Thompson\nBassoon – Sandy Wilson\nSaxophone – Troy Linsley, Glen Gillis\nHorn – Samuel Dmyterko\nTrumpet – Eric Woodsworth\nTrombone – David Dick\nPercussion – Andra Wist\nHarp – Keri Zwicker\nKeyboard – Michelle Aalders\n\n\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”11837″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
