  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/bd235f8d-5e4a-4556-8d9f-59c261cdafed",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/vibrant-light/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, April 15, 2023\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nBuy Your Tickets\n\n\n\nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nDinuk Wijeratne, conductor\nShawn Mativetsky, tabla\n\nConcerto for Tabla & Orchestra – Dinuk Wijeratne*\nScheherazade Op. 35 – Nikolai Rimsky-Korsakov\n\nScroll down to read the full program or click here to download the print-at-home version.\nEscape | Hope | Solidarity\n\nDinuk Wijeratne’s Tabla Concerto has been described as a vibrant and colourful work that audiences will never forget. His seamless blending of musical traditions reminds us that we have so much more in common and that music truly does bring us together. We then dive into the lush intoxicating world of Rimsky-Korsakov’s Scheherazade!\n*Denotes Canadian Composer\n \nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nA digital ticket gives you 24-hour access to the stream for $19.99\nSupporter tickets can be purchased for $35 and $50\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\n\nThe Program\nVibrant Light\nDinuk Wijeratne, conductor\nShawn Mativetsky, tabla\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\n\n \nConcerto for Tabla & Orchestra\nI. Canons, Circles\nII. Folk song: ‘White in the moon the long road lies (that leads me from my love)’\nIII. Garland of Gems\nDinuk Wijeratne\n~Intermission~\nScheherazade, Op. 35\nI. The Sea and Sinbad’s Ship (Море и Синдбадов корабль) – Largo e maestoso. Allegro non troppo\nII. The Legend of the Kalendar Prince (Рассказ царевича Календера) – Lento. Andantino. Allegro molto. Con moto\nIII. The Young Prince and The Young Princess (Царевич и царевна) – Andantino quasi allegretto. Pochissimo più mosso. Come prima. Pochissimo più animato\nIV. Festival at Baghdad. The Sea. Ship Breaks upon a Cliff Surmounted by a Bronze Horseman (Багдадский празд­ник. Море. Корабль разбивается о скалу с мед­ным всадником) – Allegro molto. Vivo. Allegro non troppo maestoso.\nNikolai Rimsky-Korsakov\nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”12247″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\n\n\nViolin 1  –  Nova Wong, Brandon Johnson, Monica Martin\nViolin 2  –  Alexa Arnyek\nViola  –  Heather WIlson\nBass  –  Cameron Breiter\nHarp  –  Keri Zwicker\nFlute/ Piccolo  –  Rowan Froh\nOboe/ English Horn  –  Carl Hofmeister\nHorn  –  Stacey Mortenson-Spokes, Samuel Dmyterko\nPercussion  –  Andra Wist, Will Martin, Brett Graham\n\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”12235″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n \n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
