    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:00PM, Tuesday, September 20, 2022\nMcNally Robinson Booksellers\n\n\n3130 8th Street East\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7H 0W2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n\n\n7:00PM, Tuesday, November 15, 2022\nMcNally Robinson Booksellers\n\n\n3130 8th Street East\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7H 0W2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n\n\n7:00PM, Tuesday, February 7, 2023\nMcNally Robinson Booksellers\n\n\n3130 8th Street East\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7H 0W2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n\n\n7:00PM, Tuesday, February 21, 2023\nMcNally Robinson Booksellers\n\n\n3130 8th Street East\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7H 0W2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n\n\n7:00PM, Tuesday, April 11, 2023\nMcNally Robinson Booksellers\n\n\n3130 8th Street East\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7H 0W2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n\n\n7:00PM, Tuesday, May 2, 2023\nMcNally Robinson Booksellers\n\n\n3130 8th Street East\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7H 0W2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n\n\n\nEntering its ninth season, the SSO is  thrilled to again partner with McNally Robinson Booksellers for Music Talk from McNally…and after two years of being virtual, we’re thrilled to say that we’re back to having an in-person audience!\nJoin the SSO’s Mark Turner as he interviews our conductors and artistic partners ahead of Masters Series events – you can find them in the Travel Alcove and online at the SSO’s YouTube.\nThis year our guests include:\nSeptember & November – Judith Yan\nFebruary – Rune Bergmann and Nicolas Ellis\nApril – Dinuk Wijeratne\nMay – Nicolas Ellis\nThese events, as always, are free!\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
