    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Wednesday, April 26, 2023\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nBuy Your Tickets\n\n\n\nScroll down to read the full program, or click here for the print-at-home version.\nJoin the Fireside Singers and the Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra as they collaborate to offer their audience an entertaining evening of the most powerful choral Broadway Showstoppers! The concert will showcase engaging solos, ensembles, and overtures from your favourite Broadway musicals. This exciting collaboration promises a dynamic and memorable evening filled with hope, passion, and heart, that is certain to entertain all theatregoers.\n\nThe Program\nMusic of the Night\n\nThe Fireside Singers\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nArmand Birk, Conductor\nMarilyn Whitehead, Artistic Director\nBonnie Nicholson, Pianist & Collaborator\nKelsey Stone, Choreographer\n \nThe Hunchback of Notre Dame\nZack St. Louis, Adam Brookman, Erik Jeerakathil, Rosette Caina, Hayley Ens, Jordie Hughton, Gwenda MacPherson, Jody Coller, Trevor Wingerter, Kennedy Siba, Madison McLean.\nAlan Menken & Stephen Schwartz\nArr. Michael Kosarin, Orch. Paul Suchan\nJoseph and the Amazing Technicolor Dreamcoat\nRobin Burlingham, Jory Litt-Jukes, Sean Brandt.\nAndrew Lloyd Webber & Tim Rice\nArr. Paul Suchan\nCarousel/The Sound of Music\nMadison McLean, Colby McCormac.\nRichard Rogers & Oscar Hammerstein II\nArr. Mark Hayes\nCats\nKristin Siba, Danielle Santo, Meaghan Dormuth.\nAndrew Lloyd Webber, Trevor Nunn, & T.S. Eliot\nArr. Kennedy Siba\nFiddler on the Roof\nJerry Bock & Sheldon Harnick\nArr. Herbert Baumel\nMamma Mia\nNora Rittinger, Robyn Knight, Sarah Manafo, Meaghan Dormuth.\nBenny Anderson & Bjorn Ulvaeus\nArr. Paul Suchan\n~Intermission~\nThe Phantom of the Opera\nKennedy Siba, Jordie Hughton, Sarah Chapman, Trevor Wingerter, Sean Brandt, Jory Litt-Jukes.\nAndrew Lloyd Webber, Charles Hart & Richard Stilgoe\nArr. Paul Suchan\nMatilda\nPalmer Tastad, Clark Willoughby, Keara Van Olst, Sydney Kelln, Ella Moskal, Riley Coller.\nTim Minchin\nArr. Paul Suchan\nSunday in the Park With George\nStephen Sondheim; Arranged by Mac Huff\nOrch. Paul Suchan\nLes Misérables\nErik Jeerakathil, Andrew Yang, Sean Brandt, Zack St. Louis, Jory Litt-Jukes, Trevor Wingerter, Hayley Ens, Kristin Siba, Madison McLean, Jordie Hughton, Rob Armstrong, Nicole Wingerter.\nClaude-Michel Schonberg; Edited by Stephen Metcalfe & Peter Washetll\nArr. Paul Suchan\n \nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”12274″]\nThe Fireside Singers\nIsabelle Adams\nSam Alexander\nAndrea Armstrong\nRob Armstrong\nMary Battersby\nSean Brandt\nAdam Brookman\nRobin Burlingham\nRosette Caina\nSarah Chapman\nJody Coller\nRylie Coller\nZoey Coller\nStacey Dereniwsky\nMeaghan Dormuth\nHayley Ens\nSteve Ens\nRachel Glines\nCorrine Gogal\nJane Goodale\nRobin Grey\nSage Grey\nJohn Guselle\nJulia Herman\nLaura Herman Ellen Herrick\nIan Hinther-Bennett\nJordie Hughton\nCatherine Hui\nBrenda Hyland\nErik Jeerakathil\nSydney Kelln\nSusan Kesler\nSarah Kierstead\nRobyn Knight\nJory Litt-Jukes\nCamdyn Leverick\nCooper Loshack\nJake Loshack\nSarah Manafo\nShauna Matiko\nColby McCormac\nShaquille McGonigle\nMadison McLean\nGwenda MacPherson\nElla Moskal\nQuinn Newby\nJennine Redl\nAubrie Rittinger\nNora Rittinger Paulina Salisbury\nDanielle Santo\nJanet Sedgewick\nDeena Shyluk\nKennedy Siba\nKristin Siba\nSteph Siba\nZack St. Louis\nMarilyn Stevens\nWolf Stone\nTammy Sweeny\nPalmer Tastad\nAmy-Leigh Thiessen\nDavid Thiessen\nDamon Tupper\nCaitlyn Ursaki\nKeara Van Olst\nScarlett Whitehead\nClark Willoughby\nNicole Wingerter\nTrevor Wingerter\nCeline Wingerter\nAndrew Yang\nMalea Zimmer\nClick here to read about The Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\n\n\nCello – Terry Sturge\nPiano – Bonnie Nicholson\nDrumset/ Percussion – Brett Graham\n\n[wp_show_posts id=”12289″]\nWhat’s Next at the SSO\n\n\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n \n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
