    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, April 20, 2024\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\n\nJanna Sailor, conductor\nEekwol\nFalynn Baptiste\nElyse Evangelista\nKateryna Khartova\nEileen Laverty\nMadison McLean\nEllen Nasser\nSonia Reid\nWith guest host Alex Brown\nScroll down to read the full program. Click here for a condensed print-at-home version.\nIt’s time to celebrate the exceptional female voices of Saskatoon!\nThe SSO is thrilled to team up with Maestra Janna Sailor to showcase the best pops, rock, blues, and jazz voices Saskatoon has to offer.\nPerformers include Eekwol, Sonia Reid, Falynn Baptiste, Elyse Evangelista, Eileen Laverty, Madison McLean, Ellen Nasser, Kateryna Khartova, and more!\n\nFind out what’s happening with your Orchestra! \nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nA digital ticket gives you 24-hour access to the stream for $21\nSupporter tickets can be purchased for $39\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\n\nThe Program\nYXE Divas\nJanna Sailor, conductor\nWith guest host Alex Brown\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nFeaturing\nEekwol\nBeauty\nEekwol\nArr. Geoff Li\nRunnin’ Home\nEekwol\nArr. Geoff Li\nFalynn Baptiste\nMy Love, My Life\nFalynn Baptiste\nArr. Geoff Li\nAmazing Grace\nJohn Newton\nArr. Falynn Baptiste, Orch. Geoff Li\nElyse Evangelista\nNatural Woman\nCarole King, Gerry Goffin, and Jerry Wexler\nArr. Graham Hall\nFeeling Good\nAnthony Newley and Leslie Bricusse\nArr. Geoff Li\nKateryna Khartova\n“Song to the Moon” from Rusalka\nAntonín Dvořák\n\nThe Prayer\nCarole Bayer Sager and David Foster\nArr. Bob Cerulli\nEileen Laverty\nTread Softly\nEileen Laverty\nArr. and Orch. Allan Gilliland\nWildest Dreams\nEileen Laverty\nArr. and Orch. Allan Gilliland\nMadison McLean\nThe Prayer\nCarole Bayer Sager and David Foster\nArr. Bob Cerulli\nRise Up\nAndra Day and Jennifer Desilveo\nArr. Geoff Li\nEllen Nasser\nThe Glory of Love\nBilly Hill\nArr. Taran Plamondon\nThis Town\nNiall Horan, Jamie Scott, Mike Needle, and Daniel Bryer\nArr. Geoff Li\nSonia Reid\nI Wanna Dance with Somebody\nGeorge Merrill and Shannon Rubicam\nArr. Geoff Li\n“The Impossible Dream” from Man of La Mancha\nMitch Leigh and Joe Darion\nArr. Philip J. Lang\n \nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”13077″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\nViolin  –  Brandon Johnson\nTrumpet  –  Dean McNeill\nBass Trombone – Tiess McKenzie\nPiano  –  Paul Suchan\nGuitar  – Ian Summach\nSpecial Thanks\nThanks to Dervilia art + design and Alan Anderson for lending our Divas something sparkling to wear on stage!\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”13078″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
