      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/roaring-twenties/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/roaring-twenties/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Roaring Twenties"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Celebrate the 100th anniversary of Gershwin’s Rhapsody in Blue with this concert that will remind you why the 1920s roared!"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/b6768670-3d61-4d6d-8423-acdf5cb5aad3",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/roaring-twenties/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/314d63f5-efe1-4c44-87ff-579bc9796b5d",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/roaring-twenties/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, February 10, 2024\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\n\nMélanie Léonard, conductor\nDaniel Clarke Bouchard, piano\nAmerican in Paris – George Gershwin\nRhapsody in Blue – George Gershwin\nSymphony No. 1 (“Afro-American”) – William Grant Still\n\nScroll down to read the full program, or click here to download a print-at-home version.\nIt’s time for the Twenties to roar again! From the bustle of New York streets to jazz pouring out of the cafes in Paris, the first roaring twenties were marked by fabulous parties, flappers, and art deco.\nWe’re joined by pianist Daniel Clarke Bouchard to mark the 100th anniversary of the premiere of George Gershwin’s Rhapsody in Blue.\nMaestra Mélanie Léonard leads your SSO in a program infused with the jazz and spirit of the 1920s, including Gershwin’s spectacular American in Paris!\n\nFind out what’s happening with your Orchestra! \nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nA digital ticket gives you 24-hour access to the stream for $21\nSupporter tickets can be purchased for $39\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n \n\n\nThe Program\nRoaring Twenties\nMélanie Léonard, conductor\nDaniel Clarke Bouchard, piano\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\n \nAmerican in Paris\nGeorge Gershwin\nRhapsody in Blue\nGeorge Gershwin\n~Intermission~\nSymphony No. 1 (“Afro-American”)\nI. Moderato assai. All my life long twell de night has pas’ / Let de wo’k come ez it will, / So dat I fin’ you, my honey, at last’, / Somewhaih des ovah de hill.\nII. Adagio. It’s moughty tiahsome layin’ ’roun’ / Dis sorrer-laden earfly groun’, / An’ oftentimes I thinks, thinks I / ’Twould be a sweet t’ing des to die / An’ go ’long home.\nIII. Animato. An’ we’ll shout ouah halleluyahs, / On dat mighty reck’nin’ day.\nIV. Lento, con risoluzione. Be proud, my Race, in mind and soul. / Thy name is writ on Glory’s scroll / In characters of fire. / High mid the clouds of Fame’s bright sky / Thy banner’s blazoned folds now fly, / And truth shall lift them higher.\n\nWilliam Grant Still\n \nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”12744″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\nViolin – Cherie Jarock, Lauren Dykstra, Sofia Mycyk, Richard Wang\nCello – Terry Sturge\nBass – Nevin Buehler, Emmett Fortosky\nFlute – Jennifer McAllister\nOboe – Carl Hofmeister\nBass Clarinet – Alyssa Thompson\nClarinet – Celestino de Pedro\nSaxophones – Gerard Weber, Troy Linsley, Sarah Suchan\nHorn – Stacey Mortenson-Spokes\nTrumpet – Dean McNeill\nTrombone – Erik Larson\nPercussion – Will Martin\nHarp – Keri Zwicker\nKeyboard – Michelle Aalders\nTenor Banjo – Kimbal Siebert\nSpecial Thanks\nThanks to the Edmonton Symphony Orchestra for the use of their taxi horns.\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”12728″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
