  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/43a92054-0a0b-4c83-ace0-f8d4f65a7a80",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/kinan-azmeh/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, March 2, 2024\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\n\nCosette Justo Valdés, conductor\nKinan Azmeh, clarinet\nCuriosity, Genius, and the Search for Petula Clark – Kelly-Marie Murphy\nPelléas et Mélisande – Gabriel Faure\nSymphonic Minutes – Erno Dohnanyi\nSuite for Improviser and Orchestra – Kinan Azmeh\nScroll down to read the full program, or Click Here for the Print at Home version.\nOne of the most fascinating artists of our times, the multi-faceted Kinan Azmeh has left a lasting impression of his creativity on modern classical music.\nHailed as “intensely soulful” and a “virtuoso” by The New York Times, Winner of the OpusKlassik award in 2019 clarinetist and composer Kinan Azmeh has gained international recognition for what the New Yorker has called “Spellbinding!” for his distinctive voice across diverse musical genres.\nHe joins the SSO to perform his own Suite for Improviser and Orchestra.\nMaestra Cosette Justo Valdes leads the SSO in this colourful musical adventure.\nKinan Azmeh appears by arrangement with Sciolino Artist Management.\n\nFind out what’s happening with your Orchestra! \nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nA digital ticket gives you 24-hour access to the stream for $21\nSupporter tickets can be purchased for $39\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\n\nThe Program\nKinan Azmeh with the SSO\nCosette Justo Valdés, conductor\nKinan Azmeh, clarinet\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\n\n \nCuriosity, Genius, and the Search for Petula Clark\nKelly-Marie Murphy\nPelléas et Mélisande, Op. 80\nI. Prélude\nII. Fileuse (“The Spinner”)\nIII. Sicilienne\nIV. La mort de Mélisande (“The Death of Melisande”)\n\nGabriel Fauré\n~Intermission~\nSymphonic Minutes, Op. 36\nI. Capriccio. Vivacissimo possibile\nII. Rapsodia. Andante\nIII. Scherzo. Allegro vivace\nIV. Tema con Variazione. Andante poco moto\nV. Rondo. Presto\nErnö Dohnányi\nSuite for Improviser and Orchestra\nI. Love on 139th Street in D\nII. November 22nd\nIII. Wedding\n\nKinan Azmeh\nKinan Azmeh appears by arrangement with Sciolino Artist Management\nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”12788″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\nViolin – Alexa Arnyek, Brandon Johnson, Cherie Jarock, Sofia Mycyk, Lauren Dykstra\nCello – Terry Sturge\nHarp – Keri Zwicker\nKeyboard – Michelle Aalders\nSpecial Thanks\nThanks to the Saskatoon Concert Band for the use of their crotales.\nThanks to the University of Saskatchewan Music Department for the use of their crotales.\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”12781″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
