    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, November 25, 2023\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nGrab your Seats\n\n\n\nRobert Franz, conductor\nTimothy McAllister, saxophone\n\nWhimsical Concerto of Fanciful Birds: Concerto for Saxophone, Orchestra, and Spatialized Saxophone Ensemble  – Vincent Ho\nSymphonic Dances, Op. 45 – Sergei Rachmaninoff\n\nScroll down to read the full program. You can click here to download an abridged print-at-home version.\nMaestro Robert Franz joins the SSO for a sensational night featuring Rachmaninoff’s Symphonic Dances.\nThe concert marks the world premiere of a brand-new concerto by Vincent Ho. This SSO commission, years in the making, showcases world-renowned saxophonist Timothy McAllister centre stage.\n\nFind out what’s happening with your Orchestra! \nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nA digital ticket gives you 24-hour access to the stream for $21\nSupporter tickets can be purchased for $39\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\n\nThe Program\nRachmaninoff Dances\nRobert Franz, conductor\nTimothy McAllister, saxophone\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\n \nWhimsical Concerto of Fanciful Birds: Concerto for Saxophone, Orchestra, and Spatialized Saxophone Ensemble\nI. Enchanted Migrations\nII. Angels and Mockingbirds\nIII. Urban Birds\n\nVincent Ho\n The Spatialized Saxophone Ensemble includes Gerard Weber, Troy Linsley, Glen Gillis, Ricardo Martin, Sarah Suchan, & Nathan Degenhart.\n~Intermission~\nSymphonic Dances, Op. 45\nI. Non Allegro\nII. Andante con moto. Tempo di Valse\nIII. Lento assai – Allegro vivace\n\nSergei Rachmaninoff\nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”12560″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\nViolin – Evan Barber, Monica Martin, Cherie Jarock, Sofia Mycyk\nFlute – Jennifer McAllister\nOboe – Carl Hofmeister, Tyrell Hardlotte\nClarinet – Alyssa Thompson\nBassoon – Jonathan Tait\nSaxophone – Gerard Weber, Troy Linsley, Glen Gillis, Ricardo Martin, Sarah Suchan, Nathan Degenhart\nHorn – Stacey Mortenson-Spokes\nTrumpet – Dean McNeill\nTrombone – Spencer Krips, Tiess McKenzie\nPercussion – Andra Wist, Will Martin\nHarp – Keri Zwicker\nKeyboard – Michelle Aalders\nSpecial Thanks\nThanks to the Saskatoon Concert Band for the use of their crotales.\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”12556″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
