  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/554a0ddb-3db0-4a52-9a79-de1def9de76d",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/sing-along-messiah2023/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n2:30PM, Saturday, December 16, 2023\nKnox United Church\n\n\n838 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 3H4\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave Your Spot\n\n\n\nCosette Justo Valdés, conductor \nCasey Peden, soprano\nOli Guselle, alto\nSpencer McKnight, tenor\nBrenden Friesen, bass\nSSO Chorus with Duff Warkentin\nCome and sing along to all your favourite Messiah choruses!\nA more laid-back affair, this performance features the same great soloists as the night before, and a mass choir featuring you! It’s sure to shake the rafters.\nNot wanting to sing? That’s okay too! Come watch the fun and enjoy an afternoon of Handel’s Messiah. There are always fun surprises at Sing-Along Messiah!\nWant to practice ahead of time, but don’t have a score?  You can download a digital copy for your tablet here.\nLooking for the Friday evening performance of Handel’s Messiah? Click Here\n\nFind out what’s happening with your Orchestra! \nThis performance is not available on ConcertStream.tv, but the full performance of Handel’s Messiah is starting December 17, 2023.\n\nA digital ticket gives you 24-hour access to the stream for $21\nSupporter tickets can be purchased for $39\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n \nThe Program\nSing-Along Messiah\nCosette Justo Valdés, conductor\nCasey Peden, soprano\nOli Guselle, alto\nSpencer McKnight, tenor\nBrenden Friesen, bass\nSSO Chorus, Duff Warkentin, choral conductor\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nMessiah\n1. Sinfonia – Overture2. Tenor Recitative: Comfort ye my people3. Tenor Air: Ev’ry valley shall be exalted4. Chorus: And the glory of the Lord8. Alto Recitative: Behold, a virgin shall conceive9. Alto Air and Chorus: O thou that tellest good tidings to Zion10. Bass Recitative: For behold, darkness shall cover the earth11. Bass Air: The people that walked in darkness12. Chorus: For unto us a child is born13. Pifa – Pastoral Symphony14a. Soprano Recitative: There were shepherds abiding in the field14b. Soprano Recitative: And lo, the angel of the Lord15. Soprano Recitative: And the angel said unto them16. Soprano Recitative: And suddenly there was with the angel17. Chorus: Glory to God18. Soprano Air: Rejoice greatly, O daughter of Zion19. Alto Recitative: Then shall the eyes of the blind20. Alto and Soprano Duet: He shall feed his flock21. Chorus: His yoke is easy, and his burthen is light\n~Intermission~\n22. Chorus: Behold the Lamb of God\n23. Alto Air: He was despised\n24. Chorus: Surely he hath borne our griefs\n25. Chorus: And with his stripes we are healed\n26. Chorus: All we like sheep have gone astray\n27. Tenor Recitative: All they that see him laugh him to scorn\n28. Chorus: He trusted in God\n40. Bass Air: Why do the nations so furiously rage together?\n41. Chorus: Let us break their bonds asunder\n42. Tenor Recitative: He that dwelleth in heaven\n43. Tenor Air: Thou shalt break them\n44. Chorus: Hallelujah\n45. Soprano Air: I know that my redeemer liveth\n46. Chorus: Since by man came death\n47. Bass Recitative: Behold, I tell you a mystery\n48. Bass Air: The trumpet shall sound\n53. Chorus: Worthy is the Lamb that was slain & Amen\nGeorge Frideric Handel\nCharles Jennens, librettist\nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”12642″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert  includes:\n\n Violin 1\nMichael Swan\nLillian Jen-Payzant\nMaxim Pletnev\nSamara Caldwell\nViolin 2\nOxana Ossiptchouk\nKevin MacMillan\nDrusilla Waltz\nRobert Yang\nViola\nJim Legge\nMiles Buchwaldt\nCello\nJoel MacDonald\nJohn Payzant\nBass\nTroy Morris\nKeyboard\nKerry Agnew\n\n Oboe\nErin Brophey\nKevin Junk\nBassoon\nStephanie Unverricht\nTrumpet\nAaron Bueckert\nSamuel Boyd\nTimpani\nDarrell Bueckert\nSSO Chorus\n Duff Warkentin, conductor\nSoprano\nCatherine Berntson\nKathleen Brannen\nHeidi Dick\nSusan Ens-Funk\nLynn Ewing\nMegan Grier\nLauren MacDonald\nAndrea Johnson\nAlto\nJaki Esquirol\nMorgan Esquirol\nKathryn Janzen\nLynette Janzen\nCatherine Klopoushak\nMary Loewen\nShirl Siebert\nElaine Thaller\nTenor\nTim Bangsund\nAlfonso Bolarin Guillan\nPeter Cowan\nMichael Friesen\nPeter Hooge\nDerrick Lee\nTy McKenzie\nDavid Woloschuk\nBass\nBrady Anderson\nPatrick Brannen\nJames Hawn\nJonathan Moore-Wright\nMichael Siebert\nPhil Siebert\nJeremy Wiebe\nSpecial Thanks\nThanks to Nutana Park Mennonite Church for hosting our chorus rehearsals.\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”12646″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
