        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/sask-celebration/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/abff91b3-52fc-4ee6-8b11-db162fedb5d3",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/sask-celebration/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, March 23, 2024\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\n\nWilliam Rowson, conductor \nVéronique Mathieu, violin\nGodwin Friesen, piano\nSaskatoon Youth Orchestra, Richard Carnegie, SYO Music Director\nScroll down to read the full program. Click here for a condensed print-at-home version.\nA celebration with an all-star lineup of Saskatchewan artists.\nMaestro William Rowson returns to the SSO stage to showcase the amazing talent that calls Saskatoon home. The concert opens with a brand new work by Saskatoon-born composer Andrew Kesler’s Suite for the Prairies.\nThen Véronique Mathieu, the David Kaplan Chair of Strings at the University of Saskatchewan, takes centre stage in Sibelius’s masterful Violin Concerto.\nWe close the night with a bang and the return of pianist Godwin Friesen. Friesen won the 2022 OSM Competition and now brings his award-winning performance of Prokofiev’s 3rd Piano Concerto home to Saskatoon!\n\nFind out what’s happening with your Orchestra! \nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nA digital ticket gives you 24-hour access to the stream for $21\nSupporter tickets can be purchased for $39\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n \n\n\nThe Program\nSask Celebration\nWilliam Rowson, conductor\nVéronique Mathieu, violin\nGodwin Friesen, piano\nSaskatoon Youth Orchestra, Richard Carnegie\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nSuite for the Prairies\nAndrew Kesler\nViolin Concerto in D Minor, Op. 47\nI. Allegro moderato\nII. Adagio di molto\nIII. Allegro, ma non tanto\n\nJean Sibelius\n~Intermission~\nPiano Concerto No. 3, Op. 26\nI. Andante. Allegro\nII. Tema con variazioni\nIII. Allegro, ma non troppo\n\nSerge Prokofiev\n \nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”12920″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\nViolin – Nova Wong, Brandon Johnson, Alexa Arnyek\nKeyboard – Michelle Aalders\nSaskatoon Youth Orchestra\nRichard Carnegie SYO Music Director\nTamira Aziz-Salifu, Tuba\nMehtab Bath, Viola\nHamish Bell, Percussion\nNatalie Berzolla, Violin\nCameron Breiter, Double bass\nGeorgia Bruce, Violin\nKatherine Chang, Flute\nJonathan Chen, Cello\nLuc Cunningham, Bass\nMegan Davies, Oboe\nCelestino de Pedro, Clarinet\nAda DeLathouwer, Trombone\nKarnaukh Denys, viola\nJuliana Fields, Clarinet\nGrayson Fritz, Flute/pic\nParham Golshenas, Violin\nKayley Grant, Violin\nEmily Gunson, Violin\nJulia Gunson, violin\nDaly Haas, Trumpet\nGeoffrey Hamm, Violin\nSophia Han, Flute\nTyrell Hardlotte, Oboe\nHanna Hashi, Trumpet\nMina He, Violin\nRoyce Hermanson, Trumpet\nPio Herrera, Cello\nAshlynn Hill, Flute/piccolo\nNyah Hopkins, French horn\nTina Hou, Cello\nAlexander Johnson, French Horn\nGurleen Kaur, Flute\nJames Kim, Clarinet\nMaia Kryachko, Violin\nAlara Lutz, Violin\nJose Manlapaz, Bassoon\nDmitri Masich, Percussion\nZaide Masich, Cello\nElizabeth Mortson, Trombone\nOlivia Nasr, Flute\nEszter Nemeth, Violin\nFiyinfoluwa Oyedeji, Flute\nJordyn Petryk, Violin\nKayella Robertson, Percussion\nElisha Ruo, Violin\nTailor Schubert, Violin\nGarrett Schwab, Trombone\nSable Scott, French Horn\nMaria Shevyakova, Violin\nJonathan Tait, Bassoon\nMichael Tirkajla, Violin\nSiena Tivy, Violin\nThomas Vaquer, Cello\nSabine Wagner, Oboe\nRichard Wang, Violin\nKate Wright, Violin\nMingya Yang, cello\nNialan Young, Violin\nRyan Zhang, French horn\nZiqin Zhao, Clarinet\nChelsea Zhou, Violin\nAlexandra Zhu, Cello\nAngelina Zhu, Violin\nSpecial Thanks\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”12921″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
