      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/af5c0f9f-f0c7-4ed4-9337-56807d9733f4",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/rachmaninoff-romance/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, October 21, 2023\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\n\nJudith Yan, conductor \nLucille Chung, piano\nOverture to La Forza del Destino  –Giuseppe Verdi\nRhapsody on a Theme of Paganini, Op. 43 – Sergei Rachmaninoff\nSymphony No. 7 in D Minor, Op. 70 – Antonín Dvořák\nScroll down to read the full program. You can click here to download an abridged print-at-home version.\nMaestro Judith Yan has stepped in last minute to lead us in a night of lush romantic music.\nInternationally renowned pianist Lucille Chung makes a long-awaited debut with the SSO in a performance of Rachmaninoff’s deeply passionate Rhapsody on a Theme of Paganini, Op. 43.\nYan closes out the show with the SSO performing Dvořák’s 7th Symphony. We can’t wait to share this music that the composer himself said was a work to stir the world!\n\nFind out what’s happening with your Orchestra! \nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nA digital ticket gives you 24-hour access to the stream for $19.99\nSupporter tickets can be purchased for $35 and $50\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n \n\n\nThe Program\nRachmaninoff Romance\nJudith Yan, conductor\nLucille Chung, piano\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nOverture to La Forza del Destino\nGiuseppe Verdi\nRhapsody on a Theme of Paganini, Op. 43\nSergei Rachmaninoff\n~Intermission~\nSymphony No. 7 in D Minor, Op. 70\nI. Allegro maestoso\nII. Poco adagio\nIII. Scherzo. Vivace\nIV. Finale. Allegro\n\nAntonín Dvořák\nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”12490″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\nViolin – Luke Hnenny, Cherie Jarock, Kayley Grant, Sofia Mycyk\nBass – Emmet Fortosky\nFlute – Jennifer McAllister\nOboe – Carl Hofmeister\nPercussion – Andra Wist\nHarp – Keri Zwicker\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”12492″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
