    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "To celebrate Joni Mitchell’s 80th birthday, the SSO teams up with Sarah Slean to explore music from Mitchell's albums Both Sides Now and Travelogue. "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/36eb2b01-4f14-49d4-ad0b-279a3064e373",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/a-case-of-you/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/30fb9c29-f8cc-4991-9e01-43ba556dc4eb",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/a-case-of-you/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, October 28, 2023\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nBuy Your Tickets\n\n\n\nSarah Slean Sings The music of Joni Mitchell\nKarl Hirzer, conductor\nScroll down to read the full program.\nTo celebrate Joni Mitchell’s 80th birthday, the SSO teams up with Sarah Slean to explore music from Mitchell’s albums Both Sides Now and Travelogue. \nJoni Mitchell has gained a reputation as one of the greatest musical artists of all time – it’s extra special to be able to showcase this performance here at the singer-songwriter’s hometown.\nOur 2018 performance of Mitchell’s music with Slean was a landmark first live performance of Vince Mendoza’s beautiful orchestrations – this new concert pairs favourites like A Case of You and Both Sides Now with classics like River, Blue, and Circle Game.\n\nFind out what’s happening with your Orchestra! \nBecome an SSO Streaming Subscriber to Live stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n \n\n\nThe Program\nA Case of You\nSarah Slean Sings the Music of Joni Mitchell\nKarl Hirzer, conductor\nSarah Slean, vocals\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nYou’re My Thrill\nJay Gorney & Sidney Clare\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nAt Last\nMack Gordon & Harry Warren\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nAnswer Me, My Love\nGerhard Winkler & Carl Sigman\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nThe Circle Game\nJoni Mitchell\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nRiver\nJoni Mitchell\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nWoodstock\nJoni Mitchell\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nHejira\nJoni Mitchell\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nBe Cool\nJoni Mitchell\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nSex Kills\nJoni Mitchell\nArr. Vince Mendoza\n~Intermission~\nJudgement of the Moon and Stars\nJoni Mitchell\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nA Case of You\nJoni Mitchell\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nI Wish I Were in Love Again\nLorenz Hart & Richard Rodgers\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nRefuge of the Roads\nJoni Mitchell\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nBlue\nJoni Mitchell\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nGod Must Be A Boogie Man\nJoni Mitchell\nArr. Vince Mendoza\nBoth Sides Now\nJoni Mitchell\nArr. Vince Mendoza\n \nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”12537″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\nViolin – Evan Barber, Sofia Mycyk, Kayley Grant\nCello – Terry Sturge, Jo Eggleston\nClarinet – Alyssa Thompson, Celestino de Pedro\nBassoon – Jonathan Tait\nSaxophone – Mark DeJong\nHorn – Stacey Mortenson-Spokes, Roxanne Inch, Elke Mau\nTrumpet – Dean McNeill, Hanna Hashi\nTrombone – Spencer Krips\nPercussion – Andra Wist, Brett Graham\nHarp – Keri Zwicker\nPiano – Paul Suchan\nBass – Soren Nissen\nSpecial Thanks\nThanks to the Saskatoon Concert Band for the use of their crotales.\nThanks to the Aden Bowman Collegiate Band Program for the use of their Alto Flute.\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”12526″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
