        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/torch-songs/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Torch Songs"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "One of Canada’s most loved voices joins the SSO for a special night of jazz torch songs from their upcoming album Too Good to Talk About!"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/ff485b96-8307-44de-a6ec-a3b9a6de31b9",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/torch-songs/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/04d98ef8-3c9e-4750-96b5-5b838fdd4445",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/torch-songs/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, May 25, 2024\nRemai Arts Centre – Persephone Theatre\n\n\n100 Spadina Crescent\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7K 0L3\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave Your Seats\n\n\n\nJulie Nesrallah \nJanna Sailor, conductor\nWhat happens when you take one of Canada’s greatest vocalists and storytellers and mix in some jazz and the SSO?\nYou get an unforgettable evening!\nStar of CBC’s Tempo, Julie Nesrallah teamed up with the SSO to record a new album of jazz standards and torch songs in the fall of 2022, and now you can enjoy them live in concert!\nThe album “Too Good To Talk About” comes out later in 2024.\n \n\nFind out what’s happening with your Orchestra! \nWatch the last time Julie Nesrallah joined your SSO –  An Intimate Evening with Julie Nesrallah on ConcertStream.tv\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\n\nThe Program\nTorch Songs with Julie Nesrallah\nJulie Nesrallah \nJanna Sailor, conductor\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nThis concert includes:\nBesame Mucho\nConsuelo Velázquez\nArr. Paul Suchan\nFever\nEddie Cooley and Otis Blackwell\nArr. Paul Suchan\n“Habanera” from Carmen\nGeorges Bizet\nArr. Paul Suchan\nI’ve Got You Under My Skin\nCole Porter\nArr. Paul Suchan\nI’ve Got a Crush on You\nGeorge Gershwin\nArr. Paul Suchan\nIt’s a Man\nBetty Hutton\nArr. Paul Suchan\nIt’s Too Good to Talk About Now\nBlossom Dearie\nArr. Paul Suchan\nLies of Handsome Men\nCleo Laine\nArr. Paul Suchan\nMy Funny Valentine\nRichard Rodgers and Lorenz Hart\nArr. Paul Suchan\nPeel Me a Grape\nDavid Frishberg\nArr. Paul Suchan\nThe Man That Got Away\nHarold Arlen\nArr. Paul Suchan\nThe Rose\nAmanda McBroom\nArr. Paul Suchan\n \nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”13204″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert includes:\n\nViolin 1\nMichael Swan\nDrusilla Waltz\nLillian Jen-Payzant\nViolin 2\nOxana Ossiptchouk\nKaren Bindle\nKevin MacMillan\nViola\nJim Legge\nCello\nJoel MacDonald\nJohn Payzant\nBass\nTroy Morris \n\nFlute\nJoey Zhuang\nOboe\nErin Brophey\nClarinet\nMargaret Wilson\nBassoon\nStephanie Unverricht\nHorn\nCarol-Marie Cottin\nPercussion\nBrayden Krueger\n\nSpecial Thanks\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n \nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
