  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/b75bd76b-3cc1-4eb1-98a4-bdf541851ee5",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/harry-potter-and-the-philosophers-stone-in-concert/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n1:30PM, Saturday, October 7, 2023\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nBuy Your Tickets\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, October 7, 2023\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nBuy Your Tickets\n\n\n\nRelive the film that started it all. Watch the wand choose the wizard, a troll run amok and magic mirrors in high-definition while a live orchestra performs John Williams’ iconic score. Don’t miss this once-in-a-lifetime event as Harry, Ron, Hermione and all your favorite characters return to the screen and enchant the world all over again.\nWIZARDING WORLD and all related trademarks, characters, names, and indicia are © & ™ Warner Bros. Entertainment Inc. Publishing Rights © JKR. (s23)\n \n\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\n\n\nViolin – Nova Wong, Brandon Johnson, Evan Friesen, Christina Barry, Richard Wang, Carmelle Pretzlaw, Hannah Lissel-DeCorby\nViola – Heather Wilson, Michael Hrycay, Megan Zak\nCello – Terry Sturge, Hans Deason, Sean Whelan\nBass – Warren Hay, Curtis Scheschuk, Elke Mau\nFlute – Rowan Froh\nOboe – Carl Hofmeister\nClarinet – Alyssa Thompson\nBassoon – Jonathan Tait\nHorn – Stacey Mortenson-Spokes, Bill Dust\nTrumpet – Hanna Hashi\nPercussion – Andra Wist, Will Martin, Michelle Kaminsky\nHarp – Samantha Spurrier\nKeyboards – Michelle Aalders, Kerry Agnew, Naomi Piggott-Suchan\nSpecial Thanks\nThanks to the Saskatoon Concert Band for the use of their crotales.\nThanks to the Aden Bowman Collegiate Band Program for the use of their Alto Flute.\n\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\nThanks to the Saskatoon Concert Band for the use of their crotales.\n\nThanks to the Aden Bowman Collegiate Band Program for the use of their Alto Flute.\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
