  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/484b3c75-3329-41e7-91bc-b26d20404ac6",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/music-talk-from-mcnally-9/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:00PM, Tuesday, October 17, 2023\nMcNally Robinson Booksellers\n\n\n3130 8th Street East\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7H 0W2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n\n\n7:00PM, Tuesday, February 6, 2024\nMcNally Robinson Booksellers\n\n\n3130 8th Street East\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7H 0W2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n\n\n7:00PM, Tuesday, February 27, 2024\nMcNally Robinson Booksellers\n\n\n3130 8th Street East\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7H 0W2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n\n\n7:00PM, Tuesday, March 19, 2024\nMcNally Robinson Booksellers\n\n\n3130 8th Street East\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7H 0W2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n\n\n7:00PM, Tuesday, April 30, 2024\nMcNally Robinson Booksellers\n\n\n3130 8th Street East\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7H 0W2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\n\n\n\nThe SSO is thrilled to again partner with McNally Robinson Booksellers for Music Talk from McNally…and after two years of being virtual, we’re thrilled to say that we’re back to having an in-person audience!\nJoin the SSO’s Mark Turner as he interviews our conductors and artistic partners ahead of Masters Series events – you can find them in the Travel Alcove and online at the SSO’s YouTube.\nThis year our guests include:\nOctober – Judith Yan\nLearn more about our special chat on November 21st with conductor Robert Franz and composer Vincent Ho.\nFebruary -Mélanie Léonard, Cosette Justo Valdés – The February 27 event has been cancelled.\nMarch – William Rowson\nApril – Judith Yan\n \nThese events, as always, are free!\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
