    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/8b7b5207-4f42-4188-b5de-496c28f466d8",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/discovering-the-amatis/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/2ff3020a-4997-4665-b28c-8f47c3ae252c",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/discovering-the-amatis/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n3:00PM, Sunday, October 15, 2023\nConvocation Hall\n\n\n107 Administration Place\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7N 5A2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\n\nThe Amati String Instruments will be presented in a concert series featuring various musicians beginning in fall 2023 until spring 2024. The series has been curated by Dr. Véronique Mathieu (D.Mus), associate professor of Violin and the David L. Kaplan Chair in Music, a position made possible by a $2-million donation from USask alumni Xiaoping (Bob) Xu (MA’92, LLB’17) and Ling Chen (MA’90).\nPlease note: Concert Season Pass Holders will be able to attend all Discovering the Amatis concerts, as well as be invited to a reception with the artists following each performance.\nFind information about each show below:\nOct. 15, 2023: The Voice of the Cello\nFeaturing: Stéphane Tétreault, cello & Sandra Murray, piano\nConcert is presented in partnership with the Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra and Prairie Debut.\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
