    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/0feac9a9-c7a3-4721-9b38-665dd1a08789",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/bon-appetit/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n2:00PM, Sunday, January 21, 2024\nGrosvenor Park Church\n\n\n407 Cumberland Ave S\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7H 2L3\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nFREE EVENT\n\n\n\nBased on two episodes from Julia Child’s show “The French Chef”, Bon appétit! was written as a one-act opera, or a “monologue for mezzo-soprano and chamber ensemble.”\nSaskatoon’s own Oli Guselle takes to the stage to bake us a cake as Julia Child, backed by the Saskatoon Symphony’s Wind Quintet and pianist Kerry Agnew.\nThis concert is presented in partnership with Saskatoon Opera.\nFind out what’s happening with your Orchestra! \nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\nThe Program\nBon Appétit!\nOli Guselle, mezzo-soprano\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nBon Appétit! – A Musical Monologue\nComposed by Lee Hoiby\nLibretto by Julia Child, adapted by Mark Shulgasser\nPresented under license from G. Schirmer Inc., copyright owners.\n Aires Tropicales\nI. Alborada\nII. Son\nIII. Habanera\nIV. Vals Venezolano\nV. Dizzyness\nVI. Contradanza\n\nPaquito d’Rivera \nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”12688″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert  includes:\nJoey (Xiaoying) Zhuang – principal flute\nErin Brophey – principal oboe\nMargaret Wilson – principal clarinet\nStephanie Unverricht – principal bassoon\nCarol-Marie Cottin – principal horn\nKerry Agnew – piano\nSpecial Thanks\nTo the Saskatoon Opera partnering with us for this show.\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”12691″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n \n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
