    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Illuminare"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Celebrating Light on February 4, 2024 at St John's with The Greystone Singers and Aurora Voce. "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/5f7c15f2-417d-42d2-9485-398b4200acf8",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/illuminare/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/b36b87a6-d384-4cf4-85bc-b5594e582bfc",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/illuminare/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Sunday, February 4, 2024\nSt John’s Cathedral\n\n\n 816 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7K 3H4\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\n\nThe Greystone Singers and Aurora Voce singers conducted by Dr. Jennifer Lang will be celebrating the theme of “Light” in this special concert Illuminare. This performance highlights Elaine Hagenberg’s 5-movement work Illuminare that will be featured at Carnegie Hall by these Saskatchewan singers on June 1, 2024. Special appearances include the Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra, Hussein Janmohamed conducting his own “Nur Reflections on Light”, and Dr. Steven Rayan and Anna Elliott’s work The Projection Project, an animated, light-based installation produced in celebration of USask’s Quantum Innovation Signature Area of Research.\n \nThis event has online ticket sales only. This event will not be on ConcertStream.tv.\n\nFind out what’s happening with your Orchestra! \nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n \nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
