    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/enigma/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, September 21, 2024\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\n\nTania Miller, conductor\nSara Davis Buechner, piano\nHome – Michael Oesterle*\nPiano Concerto No.1, Op.23 – Pyotr Tchaikovsky\nVariations on an Original Theme, Op. 36 (Enigma Variations) – Edward Elgar\nScroll down to read the full program. \n Click here for the print-at-home version.\nYour orchestra is celebrating the beginning of the 94th season by bringing home the incredible Maestra Tania Miller. She will lead your SSO in Elgar’s iconic Enigma Variations.\nMaking her long-awaited SSO debut, pianist Sara Davis Buechner joins your orchestra to perform Tchaikovsky’s Piano Concerto No. 1. The passionate and emotional first movement is one of the most recognizable concerto openings.\nMaestra Miller has chosen to open the concert with a piece she commissioned from friend and composer Michael Oesterle entitled Home – a fitting start to season 94!\n*Denotes Canadian composer.\n\nFind out what’s happening with your Orchestra! \nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nA digital ticket gives you 24-hour access to the stream for $22\nSupporter tickets can be purchased for $35\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\n\nThe Program\nEnigma\nTania Miller, conductor\nSara Davis Buechner, piano\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nHome\nMichael Oesterle*\n\nPiano Concerto No. 1 in B-flat Minor, Op. 23\nI. Andante non troppo e molto maestoso — Allegro con spirito\nII. Andantino semplice — Allegro vivace assai\nIII. Allegro con fuoco\nPyotr Tchaikovsky\n~Intermission~\nVariations on an Original Theme ‘Enigma’, Op.36\nTheme (Andante)\nVariation I. L’istesso tempo “C.A.E.”\nVariation II. Allegro “H.D.S-P.”\nVariation III. Allegretto “R.B.T.”\nVariation IV. Allegro di molto “W.M.B.”\nVariation V. Moderato “R.P.A.”\nVariation VI. Andantino “Ysobel”\nVariation VII. Presto “Troyte”\nVariation VIII. Allegretto “W.N.”\nVariation IX. Adagio “Nimrod”\nVariation X. Intermezzo: Allegretto “Dorabella”\nVariation XI. Allegro di molto “G.R.S.”\nVariation XII. Andante “B.G.N.”\nVariation XIII. Romanza: Moderato “* * *”\nVariation XIV. Finale: Allegro Presto “E.D.U.”\nEdward Elgar\n*Denotes Canadian composer.\nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”12926″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\nViolin – Kayley Grant, Shabnam Abbasi, Nialan Young, Cherie Jarock, Sofia Mycyk\nCello – Terry Sturge\nBass – Nevin Buehler\nBassoon – Jonathan Tait\nHorn – Erin McVittie\nTrumpet – Hanna Hashi\nSpecial Thanks\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”13305″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
