    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, October 26, 2024\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\n\nJanna Sailor, Conductor\nCris Derksen, cello/composer\nZoey Roy, spoken word poet/composer\nControlled Burn – Cris Derksen*\nEver, Beautiful– Zoey Roy*\nCanada Mosaic – Jean Coulthard*\nContemplating Clouds on a Prairie Sky – Wayne Toews*\nFrenergy – John Estacio*\nScroll down to read the full program.\nMaestra Janna Sailor returns home to lead the orchestra in an all-Canadian program featuring new works by Saskatoon’s  Artist/Activist/Educator Zoey Roy, and local composer/educator Wayne Toews. The concert also includes Coulthard’s Canada Mosaic, John Estacio’s Frenergy, and a new piece by cellist/composer Cris Derksen.\nDerksen joins the SSO to perform her fiery new work Controlled Burn. Commissioned by Montréal’s Orchestre Métropolitain, it simulates the sounds of the Indigenous Peoples’s centuries-old practice of using fire to clear forest debris and protect trees and wildlife.\nZoey Roy takes to the stage with her hip-hop-inspired spoken word poetry and her piece Ever, Beautiful which has been orchestrated by fellow performer Cris Derksen.\nIt’s a celebration of Canadian excellence!\n*Denotes Canadian Composer\n\nFind out what’s happening with your Orchestra! \nLive stream this performance on ConcertStream.tv\n\nA digital ticket gives you 24-hour access to the stream for $22\nSupporter tickets can be purchased for $35\nSSO Streaming Subscription gives you unlimited access to live streams and concert films on demand\nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\n\n\nThe Program\nControlled Burn\nJanna Sailor, Conductor\nCris Derksen, cello/composer\nZoey Roy, spoken word poet/composer\nSaskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nFrenergy\nJohn Estacio*\nCanada Mosaic\n   I. Lullaby for a Snowy Night\n   II. Mam’zelle Québécoise\n   V. The Contented House\n   VI. Billowing Fields of Golden Wheat\nJean Coulthard*\nControlled Burn\nCris Derksen*\nIntermission\nContemplating Clouds on a Prairie Sky\nWayne Toews*\nEver, Beautiful\n   Listen to the Water\n   Back in the Alley\n   The Tree\n   Answered Prayers\n   Up and Coming\n   My Muse\n   Guided Cookie\nZoey Roy*\nOrch. Cris Derksen*\nProgram order is subject to change.\n*Denotes Canadian composer.\nThe Artists\n[wp_show_posts id=”12929″]\nClick here to read about your Orchestra!\nThis concert also includes:\n \nSpecial Thanks\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”13322″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
