  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/b7e9fed6-c8e6-494b-90e7-ec63649c8cc6",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/sleeping-beauty/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/9b5b2cf0-8645-4063-a000-c11fc3c7819c",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/WPHeader"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/sleeping-beauty/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/f7116e31-7020-447f-971b-f17de7dd73ec",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/sleeping-beauty/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, February 15, 2025\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\nRead The Program\n\nJudith Yanconductor\nTimothy Chooiviolin\n\n\nScottish Fantasy, Op. 46Max Bruch\nI Introduction: Grave. Adagio cantabile\nII Scherzo: Allegro\nIII Andante sostenuto\nIV Finale: Allegro guerriero\nINTERMISSION\nThe SSO Sleeping Beauty SuitePyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky – Compiled by Judith Yan\nINTRODUCTION – The Baptism of Princess Aurora\nIntroduction\nNo. 1 Marche\nNo. 4 Finale – Entrance of Carabosse – Entrance of the Lilac Fairy\nACT I – Princess Aurora’s Ball\nNo. 6 Valse – Princess Aurora’s 16th Birthday\nNo 7 Scène – Entrance of Aurora\nNo. 8 Rose Adagio – Princess Aurora dances with 4 Princes\nNo. 9 Finale – The Curse of Carabosse – Lilac Fairy casts a spell\nACT II – Prince Désiré and Princess Aurora\nNo. 15 – Lilac Fairy shows Prince Désiré a vision of the Princess\nNo. 19 & No.20 – Prince defeats Carabosse – and wakes Princess Aurora\nACT III – The Wedding of Princess Aurora and Prince Désiré\nNo. 30 Finale & Apothéoses\n\n\nViolinist Timothy Chooi returns for a concert filled with music that’s perfect for you and your valentine. Led by Maestra Judith Yan, Chooi and your orchestra will wow us with Bruch’s stunning Scottish Fantasy. The romantic evening is made complete with selections from Tchaikovsky’s ballet The Sleeping Beauty curated by ballet aficionado Yan herself.\nTimothy Chooi is represented by Colbert Artists Management, Inc..  www.colbertartists.com\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
