  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/cced24fd-0816-43b5-96d2-d1452d0f5789",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/once-upon-a-time/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, January 25, 2025\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\nRead The Program\n\nKarl Hirzerconductor\nLisa Livesay\nWhitney Claire Kaufman\nAaron Phillips\nAndrew Johnson\n\n\nFantasmic!Composed, Arranged, and Orchestrated by Bruce Healey\n© 1992 Walt Disney Music Company\n“When Will My Life Begin”Music by Alan Menken |  Lyrics by Glenn Slater | Arranged by Michael Starobin\n© 2014 Walt Disney Music Company,  and Wonderland Music Company, Inc.\nSongs from Disney’s The Little MermaidMusic by Alan Menken | Lyrics by Howard Ashman | Arranged by A. Menken, R. Merkin, T. Pasatieri and T. Ricketts\n© 1990 Wonderland Music Co., Inc. (BMI)\n“Part of Your World”, “Under the Sea”, “Kiss the Girl”, “Happy Ending”\n“How Far I’ll Go”Words and Music by Lin-Manuel Miranda\n© 2016 Walt Disney Music Company\n“Go the Distance”Music by Alan Menken | Lyrics by David Zippel | Arranged by Brad Kelley\n© 1997 Wonderland Music Co., Inc. (BMI) & Walt Disney Music Company (ASCAP)\n“We Don’t Talk About Bruno”Words and Music by Lin-Manuel Miranda\n© 2021 Walt Disney Music Company\nFrozen MedleyWords and Music by Kirsten Anderson-Lopez and Robert Lopez | Underscore composed by Christopher Best |  Orchestrations by Dave Metzger | Adapted by Ted Ricketts\n© 2013 Wonderland Music Company, Inc.\n“The Great Thaw”, “Elsa and Anna”, “Do You Want to Build a Snowman?”, “For the First Time in Forever”, “In Summer”, “Let It Go”\nINTERMISSION\nDisney’s Beauty and the Beast SuiteMusic by Alan Menken | Lyrics by Howard Ashman | Arranged by Danny Troob and Franck van der Heijden | Edited by Ted Ricketts\n© 1992 Wonderland Music Co., Inc. (BMI) & Walt Disney Music Company (ASCAP)\n“Transformation”, “Belle”, “Be Our Guest”, “Beauty and the Beast”\nA Dream is a Wish Medley (songs from Disney’s Cinderella)Music and Lyrics by Mack David, Al Hoffman, and Jerry Livingston | Arranged by Joe Dubin, Sid Fine, and Ted Ricketts\n© 1948 Walt Disney Music Company (ASCAP)\n“Trust in Me (The Python’s Song)”Words and Music by Richard Sherman and Robert B. Sherman\n© 1966 Walt Disney Music Company\n© 1990 Wonderland Music Co., Inc.\n“Be Prepared”Music by Elton John | Words by Tim Rice\n© 1994 Wonderland Music Co., Inc.\nPirates of the Caribbean SuiteMusic by Klaus Badelt | Arranged by Ted Ricketts\n© 2003 Walt Disney Music Company (ASCAP)\nSongs from Disney’s The Lion KingMusic by Elton John | Lyrics by Tim Rice | Score by Hans Zimmer | Arranged by Brad Kelley and Ted Ricketts\n© 1994 Wonderland Music Co., Inc. (BMI)\n“King of Pride Rock (This Land)”, “Nants Ingonyama”, “Circle of Life”, “I Just Can’t Wait to be King”, “Can You Feel the Love Tonight?”, “Pridelands (Busa)”\n\n\nJoin us for a magical journey into storytelling and music as only the timeless tales of Disney can evoke.  Brought to life by the talents of four Broadway calibre singers, The Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra, and featuring high resolution Animated Feature Film sequences, Disney in Concert Once Upon a Time explores iconic moments, plot twists and feats of daring heroics from Encanto, Frozen, Beauty and the Beast, Cinderella, The Little Mermaid, Tangled, The Lion King and many more.  \nPresentation authorized by Disney Concerts  All rights reserved\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
