    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Lost Birds"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "We celebrate 40 years with concertmaster Michael Swan and Evan Mitchell conducts Christopher Tin's choral masterpiece The Lost Birds."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/86625758-1c5c-45fd-a1a0-8c570e9d3850",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/the-lost-birds/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/056c9fa0-840f-4be9-b197-a671d18c69a3",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/WPHeader"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/the-lost-birds/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/222c2fc1-3f10-461e-a93c-2c93fa32e788",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/the-lost-birds/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, March 8, 2025\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\nRead The Program\n\nEvan Mitchellconductor\nMichael Swanviolin\nUniversity of Saskatchewan Greystone SingersDr. Jennifer Lang\nAurora VoceDr. Jennifer Lang\n\n\nCome Closer: Songs on Texts by Elizabeth KrehmRyan Trew\nIntermezzo\nViolin Concerto No. 1 in F-sharp Minor, Op. 14Henri Wieniawski\nI. Allegro moderato\nII. Preghiera: Larghetto\nIII. Rondo: Allegro giocoso\nINTERMISSION\nThe Lost BirdsChristopher Tin\nI. Flocks a Mile Wide\nII. The Saddest Noise\nIII. Bird Raptures\nIV. A Hundred Thousand Birds\nV. Wild Swans\nVI. Intermezzo\nVII. Thus In The Winter\nVIII. There Will Come Soft Rains\nIX. All That Could Never Be Said\nX. I Shall Not See The Shadows\nXI. In The End\nXII. Hope Is The Thing With Feathers\n\n\nWe’re celebrating 40 seasons with our very own concertmaster Michael Swan! He’ll take centre stage to perform Wieniawski’s Violin Concerto No. 1 in F-sharp Minor, Op. 14\nConductor Evan Mitchell leads your SSO, and choir, in Christopher Tin’s moving choral work The Lost Birds. Sweeping and elegiac, it’s a haunting tribute to those soaring flocks that once filled our skies, but whose songs have since been silenced.\nSpecial thank you to Anthonys Fashion for supporting concertmaster Michael Swan for this concert.\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
