  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/14db75c0-9685-4e57-8a8b-1152b904926d",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/chopin-and-the-new-world/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, May 3, 2025\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave Your Seats\n\n\nRead The Program\n\nTania Millerconductor\nJerry Hupiano\n\n\nCitius, Altius, Fortius!Maxime Goulet\nPiano Concerto No. 1 in E Minor, Op. 11Frédéric Chopin\nI. Allegro maestoso\nII. Romance. Larghetto\nIII. Rondo. Vivace\nINTERMISSION\nSymphony No. 9, Op. 95Antonín Dvořák\nI. Adagio — Allegro molto\nII. Largo\nIII. Molto vivace\nIV. Allegro con fuoco\n\n\nAfter his triumphant orchestral debut with us in 2021, pianist Jerry Hu returns home to perform Chopin’s Piano Concerto No. 1 in E Minor, Op. 11. Led by Maestra Tania Miller, your SSO will finish our mainstage series with Dvořák’s Symphony No. 9, Op. 95 (“New World”) and Goulet’s Citius, Altius, Fortius!\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
