    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Wednesday, October 16, 2024\nThe Roxy Theatre\n\n\n320 20th Street West\nSaskatoon, SK S7M 0X2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\n7:30PM, Thursday, October 17, 2024\nThe Roxy Theatre\n\n\n320 20th Street West\nSaskatoon, SK S7M 0X2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave your Seats\n\n\n\nIt’s the return of Silence is Golden!\nExperience the classic 1925 silent horror film adaptation of The Phantom of the Opera with a live soundtrack provided by digital accordionist Michael Bridge in Saskatoon’s iconic Magic Lantern Roxy Theatre. \nMichael Bridge is a 21st-century musical maverick—toppling popular expectations of what it is to be a professional accordionist. He’s created custom programs for his digital accordion that allow him to patch in sounds you’ve never heard his instrument make, from drums to lasers, choirs to synths, and so much more. \nHe’ll create a stunning soundtrack live while you enjoy The Phantom of the Opera on the big screen!\n\nFind Your Next Great Night Out! \nSupport your orchestra by donating today!\nThe Artist\n[wp_show_posts id=”13389″]\nSpecial Thanks\n\nClick here to learn more about our Partners.\n\nProgram Notes\n[wp_show_posts id=”13378″]\nWhat’s Next\n\nA Change is Gonna Come7:30PM Sat, Apr 11, 2026Save Your SeatsAfter Dark8:00PM Sat, Apr 18, 2026Save Your SeatsThe Traveller7:30PM Sat, May 02, 2026Save Your SeatsJames Ehnes in Recital7:30PM Wed, May 06, 2026Save Your SeatsMothers' Day2:00PM Sun, May 10, 2026FREE EVENTFinding Light7:30PM Sat, May 30, 2026Save Your SeatsCroon8:00PM Mon, Jul 06, 2026Save Your SeatsHarry Potter and the Goblet of Fire™ in Concert1:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats7:30PM Sat, Oct 10, 2026Save Your Seats\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
