  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/b4f2d7c7-9266-4382-9cd6-5cc2b3ff76bf",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/is-that-my-voice/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n10:00AM, Friday, September 27, 2024\nNutrien Wonderhub\n\n\n950 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 3H6\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nRegister\n\n\n11:15AM, Friday, September 27, 2024\nNutrien Wonderhub\n\n\n950 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 3H6\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nCancelled\n\n\n10:00AM, Saturday, September 28, 2024\nNutrien Wonderhub\n\n\n950 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 3H6\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSOLD OUT\n\n\n11:15AM, Saturday, September 28, 2024\nNutrien Wonderhub\n\n\n950 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 3H6\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nRegister\n\n\n\nOur first Time for Toddlers of the season explores all the sounds our voices can make. High, low, loud, soft, long, or short there are so many things our voices can do.\nSpecial guests soprano Chelsea Mahan Jeanson and collaborative pianist Kerry Agnew lead this Time for Toddlers class.\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
