        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/handels-messiah-3/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Friday, December 12, 2025\nKnox United Church\n\n\n838 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 3H4\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave Your Seats\n\n\nRead The Program\n\nKarl Hirzerconductor\nCasey Pedensoprano\nAndrea Ludwigmezzo-soprano\nSpencer McKnighttenor\nJayden Burrowsbass\nSSO Chorus\n\n\nMessiahGeorge Frideric Handel\n\n\nKarl Hirzer’s fall residency with the SSO wraps up as he returns for Handel’s Messiah.\nWith an all-Saskatchewan line of soloists and the SSO Chorus, we continue Saskatoon’s longest running holiday tradition.\nIf you saw last year’s Messiah, you know you’ll want to grab your seats soon – and if you missed it…don’t let this uplifting experience pass you by!\nLooking for Sing-Along Messiah? You can find it here.\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
