      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/bach-khayyam/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Bach &amp; Khayyam"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Even if more than 600 years separates the lives of Bach and Khayyam, these two genius were made to meet each other. Constantinople creates a dialogue, with the spiritual songs and arias of JS Bach in dialogue with poems of Omar Khayyam sung in Persian."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/1efa01e1-ffdd-4f01-b1e4-975546babfc1",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/bach-khayyam/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/8293a7f5-1c1a-41cd-b43c-00b9b210c52d",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/WPHeader"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/bach-khayyam/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/8fba1e5e-40b9-45f6-b541-f34c5d5ce085",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/bach-khayyam/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Thursday, February 5, 2026\nThe Broadway Theatre\n\n\n715 Broadway Ave\nSaskatoon, SK S7N 1B3\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave Your Seats\n\n\n\nConstantinople\n\n\nEven if more than 600 years separates the life of John-Sebastien Bach (1685 -1750) and Omar Khayyam (1048 -1131), these two genius were made to meet each other.  Their visions of the world, as a perfect match of mathematics mastery and a super high level of spirituality, bring these two men in a delightful dialogue and traces a clear path to the sublime. In this program Constantinople brings these two artists into a dialogue, where the sacred and spirituality transcend borders. For this new creation Constantinople proposes arrangements of some of the most beautiful spiritual songs and arias of JS Bach in dialogue with poems of Omar Khayyam sung in Persian and responding to Bach’s songs.   \nClick here for more details about the show and Constantinople.\n\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
