        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/nat-geo-1024x1024-1.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/endDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2025-11-22T21:30:00-06:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/secrets-of-the-whales/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/secrets-of-the-whales/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Secrets of the Whales"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "From Academy Award®-winning filmmaker James Cameron, the Disney+ original series SECRETS OF THE WHALES features the work of acclaimed National Geographic photographer Brian Skerry. As a concert experience, this show includes highlights from the series paired with the extraordinary power of a live orchestra."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/ae5d876a-283b-4bba-a84d-0dd1185d80fc",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/secrets-of-the-whales/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/7bb98f40-709c-42b0-afa3-3b0ecc52a9ed",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/WPHeader"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/secrets-of-the-whales/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/7087a4fb-7b57-44a8-8591-f92d3fdf387e",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/secrets-of-the-whales/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, November 22, 2025\nTCU Place, Sid Buckwold Theatre\n\n\n35 – 22nd Street East\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0C8\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSave Your Seats\n\n\nRead The Program\n\nMonica Chenconductor\nPeter StoicheffNarrator\n\n\nFrom the creative genius of Academy Award®-winning filmmaker and National Geographic Explorer at Large James Cameron and acclaimed National Geographic Explorer and Photographer Brian Skerry, the Disney+ original series Secrets of the Whales takes audiences on an epic journey into the lives of whales, revealing that they are far more like us than ever imagined. \nFilmed over a period of three years across 24 global locations, Secrets of the Whales submerges audiences deep into the lives of five different whale families: orcas, humpbacks, belugas, narwhals, and sperm whales. Witness the incredible and tender moments as these majestic creatures make lifelong friendships, teach clan heritage and traditions to their young, and grieve deeply for the loss of loved ones—just like us.\nAs a concert experience, Secrets of the Whales features highlights from the four-part series paired with the triumphant performance of a live symphony orchestra.\nThis performance is conducted by Monica Chen and narrated by University of Saskatchewan President, Peter Stoicheff.\nAbout the Composer\nAfter she was born, Raphaelle Thibaut suffered from a series of severe ear issues that led to single-sided deafness. At age 4, following doctor’s recommendation, she started an intense piano practice. Music became her path to recovery.  In 2015, after four years leading marketing at Google in Europe, she decided to pursue her lifelong passion for music and film scoring.\nRaphaelle has been a composer for global brands and major Hollywood productions like Incredibles 2 and The Act.\nAdd this show to your subscription package and save!\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
