  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/a5fe8a4f-d92a-485f-b611-11db80cb75d3",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/a-time-travellers-musical-journey/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n10:00AM, Saturday, March 15, 2025\nNutrien Wonderhub\n\n\n950 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 3H6\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nRegister\n\n\n11:15AM, Saturday, March 15, 2025\nNutrien Wonderhub\n\n\n950 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 3H6\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nRegister\n\n\n\nA Time Traveller’s Musical Journey\nwith the Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra\nMarch 15, 2025 • 10:00 AM & 11:15 AM\nExplore music through the ages with the Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra! We’ll travel through time exploring music written more than a thousand years ago, to music written just yesterday.\nWith program animateur Jennifer McAllister, you and your family will meet the members of the woodwind quintet and the family of string instruments.\nThis interactive show is made with kids aged 2-9 in mind. They will learn about rhythm and movement, how the instruments work and a bit of history about the music that those instruments can play.\nMusic featured in this show includes the following composers:\n\nMaddalena Casulana – Italy – Renaissance Era\nJohann Sebastian Bach – Germany – Baroque Era\nWolfgang Amadeus Mozart – Austria – Classical Era\nLouise Farrenc – France – Romantic Era\nWilliam Grant Still – USA – Modern Era\nLia Pas – Canada – Modern Era\n\nRegistration and tickets are available by clicking here. Proceeds support Wonderhub’s educational programming.\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
