  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/87e54a06-867a-4caf-b246-41f33e12735d",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/community-screening-ever-beautiful/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:00PM, Thursday, July 10, 2025\nRemai Modern – SaskTel Theatre\n\n\n102 Spadina Crescent E\nSaskatoon, SK S7K 0L3\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nFREE EVENT\n\n\n\nWe’re showing 4 concert films on the big screen at the Remai Modern! Starting July 10th, join us each Thursday at the Remai for a free viewing of some of our greatest moments of the past season.\nThis concert film features two of the Saskatoon Symphony Orchestra’s most memorable guest artists from their 94th Season.\nMaking her long-awaited SSO debut, pianist Sara Davis Buechner joined your orchestra on September 21, 2024 to perform Tchaikovsky’s Piano Concerto No. 1. The passionate and emotional first movement is one of the most recognizable concerto openings. The second half features Zoey Roy taking the stage with her hip-hop-inspired spoken word poetry and her piece Ever, Beautiful which has been orchestrated by composer Cris Derksen. This performance took place on October 26, 2024.\nThe SSO first launched streaming of their concerts during the 2020 lockdown. Since then more than 600,000 people in 57 countries have experienced SSO streaming performances. Having garnered a reputation of innovation and remarkable programming, the SSO’s 94th season was its biggest and best yet. The concert films featured in this partnership with Remai Modern showcase four concert films from the SSO’s now 60+ concert film collection available at http://ConcertStream.tv\n \nDuration: 70 Minutes\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
