      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "All Beethoven"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Renowned cellist Johannes Moser is joined by superstar pianist Marc-André Hamelin for a concert featuring works for cello and piano by Ludwig van Beethoven."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/6e718074-65e6-49d6-be30-718e1bc1ac42",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/Blog"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/all-beethoven/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/b50ecc27-401d-4a2b-adf1-53c31c893515",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/WPHeader"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/all-beethoven/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.saskatoonsymphony.org/temporary/117ccaa9-7f38-464a-808d-e6cf31cad42b",
    "@type": [
      "https://schema.org/CreativeWork"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://saskatoonsymphony.org/event/all-beethoven/"
      }
    ],
    "https://schema.org/text": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Thursday, February 25, 2027\nConvocation Hall\n\n\n107 Administration Place\nSaskatoon, Saskatchewan S7N 5A2\nGoogle Maps Directions\n\n\nSubscribe and Save\n\n\n\nJohannes Mosercello\nMarc-André Hamelinpiano\n\n\nCello Sonata No. 4 in C Major, Op. 102, No. 1Ludwig van Beethoven\nCello Sonata No. 3 in A Major, Op. 69Ludwig van Beethoven\nCello Sonata No. 2 in G minor, Op. 5, No. 2Ludwig van Beethoven\nCello Sonata No. 5 in D Major, Op. 102, No. 2Ludwig van Beethoven\n\n\nTwo greats meet on stage for one special concert.\nRenowned cellist Johannes Moser is joined by superstar pianist Marc-André Hamelin for a concert featuring works for cello and piano by Ludwig van Beethoven. \n“…bravura flourishes of the strapping and exuberant…Johannes Moser” The New York Times\n“Melodic fragments were subtly shaded with minute variations of dynamics and tonal color. Moser deliberately paced the long cadenza, assaying the difficult leaps of register with total accuracy while allowing the music to speak directly in an unforced manner. By contrast the finale was taken at a lightning clip. Beneath the brilliance and verve of Moser’s playing, there was always expressive depth.” Miami Herald\n“A performer of near-superhuman technical prowess” (The New York Times), Marc-André Hamelin is known worldwide for his unrivaled blend of consummate musicianship and brilliant technique in the great works of the established repertoire, as well as for his intrepid exploration of the rarities of the 19th, 20th, and 21st centuries.\n\n\n\t\t"
      }
    ]
  },
