        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\t\t\t\n\n\n7:30PM, Saturday, January 15, 2022\nOnline Event\n\n\n\nPurchase Live Stream Tickets\n\n\n\nSSO Chamber Ensemble\nJanuary marks so many new beginnings and for the SSO Chamber Ensemble it marks a new chance to bring you a concert filled with musical warmth.\nAllison Miller and Max Ostic dig into the music of Pierre-Max Dubois’ Petite Suite, while the Mistral Five Wind Quintet brings you a Saskatchewan premiere performance of Jenni Brandon’s Five Frogs!\nThe performance concludes with a complete performance of Johannes Brahms’ beautiful Serenade in D Major, Opus 11. A piece that served as a new beginning for Brahms, the work reflected on the death of his friend Robert Schumann and looked to a new musical future that Brahms set out to achieve.\nScroll down to read the full program or click here to download a print-at-home version.\n[box]This performance will take place via live stream only on ConcertStream.tv\n[button link=”https://concertstream.tv/programs/newbeginninglive”]Purchase a Digital Streaming Ticket[/button]\n[button link=”https://concertstream.tv/join”]Purchase an SSO Streaming Subscription[/button]\n24 hour live stream tickets for this event are priced at $19.99, $35, $50.\nAll live stream SSO performances are available on the SSO Streaming Subscription, $99 for the entire SSO catalogue.[/box]\n\nThe Program\nNew Beginnings\nSSO Chamber Ensemble\nPetite Suite\nI. Prelude – Andante\nII. Intermede – Allegro\nIII. Cadence – Recitativo Lentement\nIV. Burlesque – Allegretto\nV. Mouvement Perpetuel – Allegro\n\nPierre Max Dubois\nFive Frogs\nI. Leaping\nII. On The Lily Pad\nIII. Swimming\nIV. Bullfrog\nV. Catching Bugs\nVI. Epilogue\n\nJenni Brandon\nSerenade No. 1, Op. 11\nI. Allegro molto\nII. Scherzo. Allegro non troppo – Trio. Poco più moto\nIII. Adagio non troppo\nIV. Minuet 1 — Minuet 2\nV. Scherzo. Allegro – Trio\nVI. Rondo. Allegro\nJohannes Brahms\n*Order subject to change.\nSSO Chamber Ensemble\nMichael Swan – Concertma